    'Uncountable noun phrase. Collocations: rent/lease office space, shared office space.',
  ),
  'move in': VocabUsage(
    'The new employees will move in on the first of the month.',
    '',
    'Karyawan baru akan mulai menempati ruangan pada tanggal satu bulan ini.',
    '',
    'Phrasal verb. Pola: move in(to) + tempat. Lawan: move out. Kata benda: move-in date.',
    'Phrasal verb. Pattern: move in(to) + place. Opposite: move out. Noun: move-in date.',
  ),
  'move out': VocabUsage(
    'Tenants must give one month\'s notice before they move out.',
    '',
    'Penyewa harus memberi pemberitahuan satu bulan sebelum pindah keluar.',
    '',
    'Phrasal verb. Pola: move out of + tempat. Lawan: move in.',
    'Phrasal verb. Pattern: move out of + place. Opposite: move in.',
  ),
  'neighborhood': VocabUsage(
    'The hotel is located in a quiet neighborhood near the river.',
    '',
    'Hotel itu terletak di lingkungan yang tenang dekat sungai.',
    '',
    'Kata benda (Amerika; Britania: neighbourhood). Pola: in the neighborhood.',
    'Noun (US; UK: neighbourhood). Pattern: in the neighborhood.',
  ),
  'spacious': VocabUsage(
    'The new meeting room is bright and spacious.',
    '',
    'Ruang rapat baru itu terang dan luas.',
    '',
    'Kata sifat untuk ruangan/bangunan. Sinonim: roomy. Lawan: cramped (sempit).',
    'Adjective for rooms/buildings. Synonym: roomy. Opposite: cramped.',
  ),
  'downtown': VocabUsage(
    'Our main office is located downtown, near the central station.',
    '',
    'Kantor pusat kami terletak di pusat kota, dekat stasiun pusat.',
    '',
    'Kata keterangan/sifat (Amerika). Pola: go downtown (tanpa \'to\'); downtown area.',
    'Adverb/adjective (US). Patterns: go downtown (no \'to\'); downtown area.',
  ),
  'listing': VocabUsage(
    'I saw a listing for a three-bedroom house on the agency\'s website.',
    '',
    'Saya melihat iklan properti rumah tiga kamar di situs web agen itu.',
    '',
    'Kata benda. Pola: a listing for + properti. Juga: daftar umum (job listings).',
    'Noun. Pattern: a listing for + property. Also: any list (job listings).',
  ),
  'blueprint': VocabUsage(
    'The architect showed us the blueprint for the new factory.',
    '',
    'Arsitek menunjukkan kepada kami cetak biru untuk pabrik baru.',
    '',
    'Kata benda. Pola: a blueprint for + bangunan/rencana. Kiasan: rencana dasar.',
    'Noun. Pattern: a blueprint for + building/plan. Figurative: a basic plan.',
  ),
  'plumber': VocabUsage(
    'We called a plumber to fix the leaking pipe in the kitchen.',
    '',
    'Kami memanggil tukang ledeng untuk memperbaiki pipa bocor di dapur.',
    '',
    'Kata benda; huruf b tidak dibaca (/plam-er/). Pekerjaannya: plumbing.',
    'Noun; the b is silent (/plum-er/). The work: plumbing.',
  ),
  'electrician': VocabUsage(
    'An electrician is coming to check the wiring in the meeting room.',
    '',
    'Seorang tukang listrik akan datang untuk memeriksa kabel di ruang rapat.',
    '',
    'Kata benda. Kaitan: electric, electrical, electricity.',
    'Noun. Related: electric, electrical, electricity.',
  ),
  'leak': VocabUsage(
    'There is a leak in the ceiling above the reception desk.',
    '',
    'Ada kebocoran di plafon di atas meja resepsionis.',
    '',
    'Kata benda dan kerja. Pola: a leak in + benda; the pipe is leaking. Juga: membocorkan informasi.',
    'Noun and verb. Patterns: a leak in + object; the pipe is leaking. Also: leak information.',
  ),
  'repair': VocabUsage(
    'The elevator will be repaired over the weekend.',
    '',
    'Lift akan diperbaiki selama akhir pekan.',
    '',
    'Kata kerja dan benda. Pola: under repair; repair work. Sinonim: fix.',
    'Verb and noun. Patterns: under repair; repair work. Synonym: fix.',
  ),
  'remodel': VocabUsage(
    'The restaurant plans to remodel its kitchen this summer.',
    '',
    'Restoran itu berencana merombak dapurnya musim panas ini.',
    '',
    'Kata kerja. Pola: remodel + ruangan/bangunan. Kata benda: remodeling. Mirip: renovate.',
    'Verb. Pattern: remodel + room/building. Noun: remodeling. Similar: renovate.',
  ),
  'refurbish': VocabUsage(
    'The old warehouse was refurbished and turned into modern offices.',
    '',
    'Gudang lama itu diperbarui dan diubah menjadi kantor modern.',
    '',
    'Kata kerja, sering pasif. Kata benda: refurbishment. Juga untuk barang: refurbished laptop.',
    'Verb, often passive. Noun: refurbishment. Also for goods: refurbished laptop.',
  ),
  'downturn': VocabUsage(
    'Many small firms closed during the economic downturn.',
    '',
    'Banyak perusahaan kecil tutup selama kemerosotan ekonomi.',
    '',
    'Kata benda. Kolokasi: economic downturn, a downturn in + sektor. Lawan: upturn.',
    'Noun. Collocations: economic downturn, a downturn in + sector. Opposite: upturn.',
  ),
  'outlook': VocabUsage(
    'The outlook for next quarter\'s sales is positive.',
    '',
    'Prospek penjualan kuartal depan positif.',
    '',
    'Kata benda. Pola: the outlook for + hal; positive/gloomy outlook. Juga: pandangan hidup.',
    'Noun. Pattern: the outlook for + topic; positive/gloomy outlook. Also: attitude.',
  ),
  'benchmark': VocabUsage(
    'Last year\'s results will serve as a benchmark for this year.',
    '',
    'Hasil tahun lalu akan menjadi tolok ukur untuk tahun ini.',
    '',
    'Kata benda dan kerja. Pola: serve as / set a benchmark; benchmark against + pesaing.',
    'Noun and verb. Patterns: serve as / set a benchmark; benchmark against + competitors.',
  ),
  'I\'ve changed my mind': VocabUsage(
    'I was going to order pizza, but I\'ve changed my mind.',
    '',
    'Tadinya aku mau pesan piza, tapi aku berubah pikiran.',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Pakai bentuk lampau atau perfect: I changed / I\'ve changed my mind. \'I change my mind\' berarti kebiasaan (sering berubah pikiran).',
    'Casual/neutral. Use past or perfect: I changed / I\'ve changed my mind. \'I change my mind\' describes a habit.',
  ),
  'On second thought': VocabUsage(
    'On second thought, let\'s take a taxi instead of the bus.',
    '',
    'Setelah dipikir-pikir lagi, kita naik taksi saja, jangan bus.',
    '',
    'Netral. Diletakkan di awal kalimat untuk mengganti keputusan sebelumnya. Versi Inggris British: \'On second thoughts\'.',
    'Neutral. Put it at the start to replace an earlier decision. British English often says \'On second thoughts\'.',
  ),
  'It\'s up to you': VocabUsage(
    '"Should we eat Thai or Japanese?" "It\'s up to you."',
    '',
    '"Kita makan Thai atau Jepang?" "Terserah kamu."',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Menyerahkan keputusan ke lawan bicara. Kalau terlalu sering dipakai bisa terdengar tidak peduli; tambahkan alasan, mis. \'I\'m happy with either\'.',
    'Casual/neutral. Hands the decision to the other person. Overused, it can sound uninterested; add something like \'I\'m happy with either\'.',
  ),
  'I don\'t mind': VocabUsage(
    '"Do you want tea or coffee?" "I don\'t mind, whatever\'s easier."',
    '',
    '"Mau teh atau kopi?" "Aku oke saja, mana yang lebih gampang."',
    '',
    'Netral. Artinya \'tidak keberatan / apa saja boleh\', bukan \'tidak peduli\'. Jawaban untuk \'Do you mind if...?\' terbalik: \'No, I don\'t mind\' = boleh.',
    'Neutral. Means \'either is OK\', not \'I don\'t care\'. Answering \'Do you mind if...?\' is reversed: \'No, I don\'t mind\' = yes, go ahead.',
  ),
  'Either is fine': VocabUsage(
    '"The red one or the blue one?" "Either is fine with me."',
    '',
    '"Yang merah atau yang biru?" "Yang mana saja boleh buatku."',
    '',
    'Netral. Hanya untuk DUA pilihan; kalau lebih dari dua pakai \'Any of them is fine\'. Variasi: \'Either one is fine\', \'Either works\'.',
    'Neutral. Only for TWO options; for more, say \'Any of them is fine\'. Variants: \'Either one is fine\', \'Either works\'.',
  ),
  'Whatever you think is best': VocabUsage(
    'I don\'t know much about cars, so do whatever you think is best.',
    '',
    'Aku tidak terlalu paham mobil, jadi lakukan saja bagaimana baiknya menurutmu.',
    '',
    'Netral/sopan. Menunjukkan kepercayaan pada penilaian orang lain, cocok ke ahli atau teman. Jangan disingkat \'Whatever!\' — itu terdengar ketus.',
    'Neutral/polite. Shows you trust the other person\'s judgement. Don\'t shorten it to \'Whatever!\', which sounds dismissive.',
  ),
  'I\'m not sure yet': VocabUsage(
    'I\'m not sure yet if I\'ll come to the party on Saturday.',
    '',
    'Aku belum yakin apakah akan datang ke pesta hari Sabtu.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pola: I\'m not sure yet + if/whether/what... Jangan bilang \'I\'m not yet sure\' di percakapan santai — benar, tapi kaku.',
    'Neutral. Pattern: I\'m not sure yet + if/whether/what... \'I\'m not yet sure\' is correct but sounds stiff in conversation.',
  ),
  'Let me think about it': VocabUsage(
    'It\'s a great offer. Let me think about it and I\'ll call you tomorrow.',
    '',
    'Tawarannya bagus. Biar kupikirkan dulu, besok kutelepon.',
    '',
    'Netral/sopan. Meminta waktu sebelum memutuskan; juga cara halus untuk menunda atau menolak. Variasi: \'Let me sleep on it\'.',
    'Neutral/polite. Asks for time before deciding; also a soft way to delay or refuse. Variant: \'Let me sleep on it\'.',
  ),
  'I can\'t decide': VocabUsage(
    'They both look delicious, I can\'t decide!',
    '',
    'Dua-duanya kelihatan enak, aku bingung memilih!',
    '',
    'Santai. Pola: I can\'t decide + between A and B / what to... Jangan pakai \'I\'m confused to choose\' — itu terjemahan harfiah yang salah.',
    'Casual. Pattern: I can\'t decide + between A and B / what to... Avoid the literal \'I\'m confused to choose\'.',
  ),
  'I\'m leaning towards': VocabUsage(
    'I\'m leaning towards the cheaper laptop, but I\'m still not sure.',
    '',
    'Aku condong ke laptop yang lebih murah, tapi masih belum yakin.',
    '',
    'Netral. Diikuti benda atau V-ing: leaning towards staying. Menunjukkan pilihan sementara, belum final. Amerika sering pakai \'toward\'.',
    'Neutral. Followed by a noun or V-ing: leaning towards staying. Shows a provisional, not final, choice. Americans often say \'toward\'.',
  ),
  'I\'ve made up my mind': VocabUsage(
    'I\'ve made up my mind: I\'m going to study in Japan.',
    '',
    'Aku sudah mantap memutuskan: aku akan kuliah di Jepang.',
    '',
    'Netral. Menegaskan keputusan sudah final dan tidak bisa dibujuk lagi. Pertanyaannya: \'Have you made up your mind?\'',
    'Neutral. Stresses that the decision is final. The question form: \'Have you made up your mind?\'',
  ),
  'Let\'s go with that': VocabUsage(
    'Okay, the hotel near the beach is cheaper. Let\'s go with that.',
    '',
    'Oke, hotel dekat pantai lebih murah. Kita pilih itu saja.',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Dipakai saat menutup diskusi dengan satu pilihan, sering di rapat. Variasi: \'Let\'s go with the first option\'.',
    'Casual/neutral. Used to close a discussion on one choice, often in meetings. Variant: \'Let\'s go with the first option\'.',
  ),
  'Let\'s do it': VocabUsage(
    '"Should we try the new climbing gym?" "Yes, let\'s do it!"',
    '',
    '"Kita coba tempat panjat tebing yang baru?" "Iya, ayo kita lakukan!"',
    '',
    'Santai. Jawaban antusias untuk ajakan atau rencana. Jangan dipakai untuk \'ayo lakukan\' perintah atasan yang formal — cukup \'Sure, I\'ll do it\'.',
    'Casual. An enthusiastic yes to a plan or invitation. For a formal task from a boss, \'Sure, I\'ll do it\' fits better.',
  ),
  'Why not?': VocabUsage(
    '"Do you want to join us for karaoke?" "Sure, why not?"',
    '',
    '"Mau ikut karaoke bareng kami?" "Boleh, kenapa tidak?"',
    '',
    'Santai. Sebagai jawaban berarti \'ya, boleh juga\'. Hati-hati: nadanya bisa terdengar setengah hati; tambahkan \'Sure\' biar ramah.',
    'Casual. As a reply it means \'yes, sure\'. It can sound half-hearted, so \'Sure, why not?\' sounds friendlier.',
  ),
  'Count me in': VocabUsage(
    'A beach trip next weekend? Count me in!',
    '',
    'Liburan ke pantai minggu depan? Aku ikut!',
    '',
    'Santai. Menyatakan ikut serta dalam rencana atau acara. Jangan bilang \'Count me\' saja.',
    'Casual. Says you want to join a plan or event. Don\'t drop the \'in\'.',
  ),
  'Count me out': VocabUsage(
    'If we\'re leaving at 5 a.m., count me out.',
    '',
    'Kalau kita berangkat jam 5 pagi, aku tidak ikut.',
    '',
    'Santai. Menolak ikut dengan nada akrab; bisa terdengar ketus ke orang yang belum dekat. Lebih halus: \'I don\'t think I can make it\'.',
    'Casual. Declines to join in a friendly way; can sound blunt with people you don\'t know well. Softer: \'I don\'t think I can make it\'.',
  ),
  'I\'ll pass': VocabUsage(
    '"Want some more cake?" "I\'ll pass, thanks. I\'m full."',
    '',
    '"Mau kue lagi?" "Tidak usah, makasih. Aku sudah kenyang."',
    '',
    'Santai. Menolak tawaran makanan, ajakan, atau giliran. Tambahkan \'thanks\' supaya tidak terdengar dingin.',
    'Casual. Declines food, an invitation or a turn. Add \'thanks\' so it doesn\'t sound cold.',
  ),
  'Maybe next time': VocabUsage(
    'I can\'t come tonight, sorry. Maybe next time?',
    '',
    'Malam ini aku tidak bisa datang, maaf. Mungkin lain kali?',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Menolak ajakan dengan halus sambil membuka kesempatan lain. Kalau tidak benar-benar berminat, jangan dipakai terus — orang akan mengajak lagi.',
    'Casual/neutral. Softly declines while leaving the door open. If you\'re truly not interested, people may keep inviting you.',
  ),
  'I\'ll let you know': VocabUsage(
    'I need to check my schedule. I\'ll let you know by Friday.',
    '',
    'Aku perlu cek jadwal dulu. Nanti kukabari paling lambat Jumat.',
    '',
    'Netral. Menjanjikan jawaban nanti. Jangan \'I\'ll let you know it\' — tanpa \'it\'; kalau ada isi, pakai \'I\'ll let you know if/when...\'.',
    'Neutral. Promises an answer later. No \'it\' at the end; to add content, use \'I\'ll let you know if/when...\'.',
  ),
  'That settles it': VocabUsage(
    'It\'s raining and the tickets are sold out, so that settles it — we\'re staying home.',
    '',
    'Hujan dan tiketnya habis, jadi beres sudah — kita di rumah saja.',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Diucapkan saat fakta baru membuat keputusan jadi jelas. Bentuk tetap; jangan diubah ke \'That is settling it\'.',
    'Casual/neutral. Said when a new fact makes the decision obvious. It\'s a fixed form; don\'t change the tense.',
  ),
  'I agree': VocabUsage(
    'I agree, the new park looks really nice.',
    '',
    'Aku setuju, taman barunya kelihatan bagus sekali.',
    '',
    'Netral. Jangan bilang \'I am agree\' — \'agree\' adalah kata kerja, jadi tanpa \'am\'. Pola: I agree with you / I agree that...',
    'Neutral. Never say \'I am agree\' — \'agree\' is a verb. Patterns: I agree with you / I agree that...',
  ),
  'I couldn\'t agree more': VocabUsage(
    '"This city needs better public transport." "I couldn\'t agree more."',
    '',
    '"Kota ini butuh transportasi umum yang lebih baik." "Aku sangat setuju."',
    '',
    'Netral. Walau bentuknya negatif, artinya setuju 100%. Pelajar sering salah paham dan mengira ini penolakan.',
    'Neutral. Despite the negative form, it means total agreement. Learners often misread it as disagreement.',
  ),
  'Exactly': VocabUsage(
    '"So we need to leave before the traffic gets bad?" "Exactly."',
    '',
    '"Jadi kita harus berangkat sebelum macet?" "Tepat sekali."',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Menegaskan lawan bicara sudah menangkap maksudmu dengan tepat. Variasi: \'Exactly right\', \'That\'s exactly what I mean\'.',
    'Casual/neutral. Confirms the other person got your point exactly. Variants: \'Exactly right\', \'That\'s exactly what I mean\'.',
  ),
  'Absolutely': VocabUsage(
    '"Can I borrow your charger?" "Absolutely, here you go."',
    '',
    '"Boleh pinjam chargermu?" "Tentu saja, ini."',
    '',
    'Netral. \'Ya\' yang kuat dan ramah. \'Absolutely not\' = sama sekali tidak. Tekanan di suku kata pertama: AB-so-lute-ly.',
    'Neutral. A strong, friendly yes. \'Absolutely not\' = definitely no. Stress the first syllable: AB-so-lute-ly.',
  ),
  'You\'re right': VocabUsage(
    'You\'re right, I should have checked the address first.',
    '',
    'Kamu benar, harusnya aku cek alamatnya dulu.',
    '',
    'Netral. Mengakui pendapat orang lain benar. Jangan tertukar dengan \'Your right\' (tulisan salah) atau \'You\'re true\' (salah; pakai \'That\'s true\').',
    'Neutral. Admits the other person is correct. Don\'t write \'Your right\' or say \'You\'re true\' (say \'That\'s true\').',
  ),
  'Good point': VocabUsage(
    'Good point — we should book the tickets early.',
    '',
    'Poin yang bagus — kita sebaiknya pesan tiket lebih awal.',
    '',
    'Netral. Mengakui ide orang lain berguna, sering di diskusi kerja atau kelas. Variasi: \'That\'s a good point\', \'Fair point\'.',
    'Neutral. Acknowledges a useful idea, common in meetings or class. Variants: \'That\'s a good point\', \'Fair point\'.',
  ),
  'Fair enough': VocabUsage(
    '"I can\'t come because I have to work." "Fair enough."',
    '',
    '"Aku tidak bisa datang karena harus kerja." "Oke deh, masuk akal."',
    '',
    'Santai. Menerima alasan orang lain walau mungkin tidak sepenuhnya setuju. Lebih umum di Inggris British dan Australia.',
    'Casual. Accepts someone\'s reason even if you don\'t fully agree. Especially common in British and Australian English.',
  ),
  'That makes sense': VocabUsage(
    'Oh, the shop is closed for a holiday. That makes sense.',
    '',
    'Oh, tokonya tutup karena libur. Itu masuk akal.',
    '',
    'Netral. Dipakai saat penjelasan terasa logis. Jangan \'It makes sense for me\' — yang benar \'It makes sense to me\'.',
    'Neutral. Used when an explanation seems logical. Say \'It makes sense to me\', not \'for me\'.',
  ),
  'Sounds good': VocabUsage(
    '"Let\'s meet at the café at seven." "Sounds good!"',
    '',
    '"Kita ketemu di kafe jam tujuh." "Oke, siap!"',
    '',
    'Santai. Jawaban paling umum untuk menyetujui rencana atau usulan, juga di chat. Bentuk lengkapnya \'That sounds good\'.',
    'Casual. The most common way to accept a plan or suggestion, also in texts. Full form: \'That sounds good\'.',
  ),
  'Sounds like a plan': VocabUsage(
    '"Pizza and a movie at my place?" "Sounds like a plan."',
    '',
    '"Piza dan nonton film di tempatku?" "Oke, sepakat."',
    '',
    'Santai. Menyetujui rencana yang baru disusun. Jangan diterjemahkan harfiah \'kedengarannya seperti rencana\' — artinya cukup \'oke, jadi begitu\'.',
    'Casual. Agrees to a plan just made. Don\'t take it literally; it simply means \'OK, let\'s do that\'.',
  ),
  'It\'s a deal': VocabUsage(
    '"I\'ll cook if you wash the dishes." "It\'s a deal!"',
    '',
    '"Aku masak kalau kamu cuci piring." "Deal!"',
    '',
    'Santai. Menyetujui tawaran atau pembagian tugas. Versi lebih pendek: \'Deal!\'. Tanya balik: \'Deal?\'',
    'Casual. Accepts an offer or a trade-off. Shorter: \'Deal!\'. To propose: \'... Deal?\'',
  ),
  'Me too': VocabUsage(
    '"I\'m really hungry." "Me too."',
    '',
    '"Aku lapar banget." "Aku juga."',
    '',
    'Santai. Hanya untuk kalimat POSITIF. Kalau kalimatnya negatif (\'I don\'t like it\'), jawab \'Me neither\', bukan \'Me too\'.',
    'Casual. Only for POSITIVE statements. For negatives (\'I don\'t like it\'), say \'Me neither\', not \'Me too\'.',
  ),
  'Me neither': VocabUsage(
    '"I don\'t like horror movies." "Me neither."',
    '',
    '"Aku tidak suka film horor." "Aku juga tidak."',
    '',
    'Santai. Membalas kalimat negatif. Kesalahan umum: \'Me too\' untuk kalimat negatif. Bisa diucapkan ni-dher atau nai-dher; formalnya \'Neither do I\'.',
    'Casual. Replies to a negative statement. Common error: \'Me too\' after a negative. Pronounced nee-ther or nye-ther; formal: \'Neither do I\'.',
  ),
  'I guess so': VocabUsage(
    '"Is it going to rain later?" "I guess so, the sky looks dark."',
    '',
    '"Nanti bakal hujan?" "Kayaknya sih iya, langitnya gelap."',
    '',
    'Santai. \'Ya\' yang kurang yakin atau kurang antusias. Nadanya bisa terdengar terpaksa; kalau setuju penuh, pakai \'Sure\' atau \'Yes\'.',
    'Casual. A doubtful or reluctant yes. It can sound unwilling, so use \'Sure\' or \'Yes\' when you fully agree.',
  ),
  'Not really': VocabUsage(
    '"Did you enjoy the film?" "Not really, it was too long."',
    '',
    '"Kamu menikmati filmnya?" "Nggak terlalu, kepanjangan."',
    '',
    'Santai. \'Tidak\' yang halus, lebih sopan daripada \'No\' saja. Biasanya diikuti alasan singkat.',
    'Casual. A soft no, gentler than a plain \'No\'. Usually followed by a short reason.',
  ),
  'I don\'t think so': VocabUsage(
    '"Is the bank open on Sunday?" "I don\'t think so."',
    '',
    '"Banknya buka hari Minggu?" "Kurasa tidak."',
    '',
    'Netral. Dalam bahasa Inggris negasinya di \'think\': \'I don\'t think it\'s true\', bukan \'I think it\'s not true\' (terdengar janggal).',
    'Neutral. English puts the negative on \'think\': \'I don\'t think it\'s true\' sounds more natural than \'I think it\'s not true\'.',
  ),
  'I\'m not so sure about that': VocabUsage(
    '"This plan will save us a lot of money." "I\'m not so sure about that."',
    '',
    '"Rencana ini bakal menghemat banyak uang." "Aku kurang yakin soal itu."',
    '',
    'Netral/sopan. Cara halus untuk tidak setuju tanpa terdengar menyerang. Lebih aman daripada \'You\'re wrong\'.',
    'Neutral/polite. A gentle way to disagree without sounding aggressive. Safer than \'You\'re wrong\'.',
  ),
  'I see your point, but...': VocabUsage(
    'I see your point, but I think the train is still faster.',
    '',
    'Aku paham maksudmu, tapi menurutku kereta tetap lebih cepat.',
    '',
    'Netral/sopan. Mengakui pendapat lawan dulu, lalu menyampaikan pendapatmu. Bagus untuk diskusi kerja dan IELTS Speaking.',
    'Neutral/polite. Acknowledges the other view before giving yours. Useful in work discussions and IELTS Speaking.',
  ),
  'I\'m afraid I disagree': VocabUsage(
    'I\'m afraid I disagree. I think we need more time to test it.',
    '',
    'Maaf, saya tidak setuju. Menurut saya kita perlu waktu lebih untuk mengujinya.',
    '',
    'Sopan/formal. \'I\'m afraid\' di sini bukan \'takut\', melainkan pelunak = \'maaf\'. Cocok untuk rapat atau atasan.',
    'Polite/formal. \'I\'m afraid\' here doesn\'t mean scared; it softens bad news. Good for meetings or talking to a boss.',
  ),
  'Let\'s agree to disagree': VocabUsage(
    'We\'ll never like the same football team, so let\'s agree to disagree.',
    '',
    'Kita tidak akan pernah suka tim bola yang sama, jadi ya sudah, kita beda pendapat saja.',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Menghentikan debat dengan damai saat tidak ada yang mau mengalah. Diucapkan dengan nada ramah, bukan kesal.',
    'Casual/neutral. Ends an argument peacefully when neither side will change. Say it in a friendly, not annoyed, tone.',
  ),
  'Can you help me?': VocabUsage(
    'Excuse me, can you help me? I can\'t find the train station.',
    '',
    'Permisi, bisa bantu saya? Saya tidak menemukan stasiun kereta.',
    '',
    'Netral. Permintaan dasar; awali dengan \'Excuse me\' ke orang asing. Lebih sopan: \'Could you help me?\'',
    'Neutral. Basic request; start with \'Excuse me\' for strangers. More polite: \'Could you help me?\'',
  ),
  'Could you do me a favor?': VocabUsage(
    'Could you do me a favor and water my plants while I\'m away?',
    '',
    'Boleh minta tolong siramkan tanamanku selama aku pergi?',
    '',
    'Netral/sopan. Jangan \'Can I ask your favor?\' atau \'Can you help me a favor?\'. Yang benar: do me a favor / ask you a favor. Ejaan British: favour.',
    'Neutral/polite. Not \'help me a favor\'; say do me a favor / ask you a favor. British spelling: favour.',
  ),
  'Can you give me a hand?': VocabUsage(
    'Can you give me a hand with these boxes? They\'re really heavy.',
    '',
    'Bisa bantu aku angkat kardus-kardus ini? Berat banget.',
    '',
    'Santai. Biasanya untuk bantuan fisik atau tugas praktis. Pola: give me a hand with + benda/V-ing.',
    'Casual. Usually for physical or practical help. Pattern: give me a hand with + noun/V-ing.',
  ),
  'Would you mind...?': VocabUsage(
    'Would you mind closing the window? It\'s a bit cold.',
    '',
    'Keberatan tidak kalau jendelanya ditutup? Agak dingin.',
    '',
    'Sopan/formal. Setelah \'mind\' pakai V-ing: Would you mind opening... Jawaban \'ya, boleh\' justru \'No, not at all\' — \'Yes\' berarti keberatan.',
    'Polite/formal. Follow \'mind\' with V-ing: Would you mind opening... To say OK, answer \'No, not at all\'; \'Yes\' means you object.',
  ),
  'Sorry to bother you': VocabUsage(
    'Sorry to bother you, but do you know where the toilets are?',
    '',
    'Maaf mengganggu, apakah Anda tahu di mana toiletnya?',
    '',
    'Sopan. Pembuka sebelum meminta sesuatu, terutama ke orang yang sedang sibuk. Variasi: \'Sorry to interrupt\'.',
    'Polite. An opener before asking for something, especially of someone busy. Variant: \'Sorry to interrupt\'.',
  ),
  'Do you have a minute?': VocabUsage(
    'Do you have a minute? I need some advice about my presentation.',
    '',
    'Ada waktu sebentar? Aku butuh saran soal presentasiku.',
    '',
    'Netral. Menanyakan apakah orang punya waktu untuk bicara atau membantu; tidak harus tepat satu menit. Variasi: \'Got a minute?\' (santai).',
    'Neutral. Asks if someone is free to talk or help; it doesn\'t mean exactly one minute. Casual: \'Got a minute?\'',
  ),
  'If it\'s not too much trouble': VocabUsage(
    'Could you send me the file again, if it\'s not too much trouble?',
    '',
    'Bisa kirim ulang filenya, kalau tidak merepotkan?',
    '',
    'Sopan. Ditambahkan di awal atau akhir permintaan agar lebih halus. Cocok untuk email dan ke orang yang lebih tua.',
    'Polite. Added at the start or end of a request to soften it. Good in emails and with older people.',
  ),
  'I could use some help': VocabUsage(
    'I could use some help in the kitchen if anyone\'s free.',
    '',
    'Aku butuh sedikit bantuan di dapur kalau ada yang senggang.',
    '',
    'Santai. \'Could use\' di sini = butuh/ingin, bukan \'bisa memakai\'. Cara tidak langsung untuk minta tolong.',
    'Casual. \'Could use\' here means \'would like/need\', not \'be able to use\'. An indirect way to ask for help.',
  ),
  'I\'d really appreciate it': VocabUsage(
    'If you could check my essay before Friday, I\'d really appreciate it.',
    '',
    'Kalau kamu bisa cek esaiku sebelum Jumat, aku akan sangat berterima kasih.',
    '',
    'Netral/sopan. Biasanya menutup permintaan: If you could..., I\'d really appreciate it. Jangan pakai \'I\'m appreciate\' — \'appreciate\' kata kerja.',
    'Neutral/polite. Often closes a request: If you could..., I\'d really appreciate it. Never \'I\'m appreciate\' — it\'s a verb.',
  ),
  'Do you need any help?': VocabUsage(
    'You look lost. Do you need any help?',
    '',
    'Kamu kelihatan bingung. Perlu bantuan?',
    '',
    'Netral. Menawarkan bantuan ke teman atau orang asing. Variasi: \'Do you need a hand?\', \'Can I help?\'',
    'Neutral. Offers help to friends or strangers. Variants: \'Do you need a hand?\', \'Can I help?\'',
  ),
  'Is there anything I can do?': VocabUsage(
    'I heard your mum is in hospital. Is there anything I can do?',
    '',
    'Aku dengar ibumu masuk rumah sakit. Ada yang bisa kubantu?',
    '',
    'Netral/sopan. Menawarkan dukungan, sering saat orang sedang kesulitan. Lebih tulus kalau disusul tawaran konkret.',
    'Neutral/polite. Offers support, often when someone is going through a hard time. Sounds more sincere with a concrete offer.',
  ),
  'Let me help you': VocabUsage(
    'That bag looks heavy. Let me help you.',
    '',
    'Tasnya kelihatan berat. Sini aku bantu.',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Menawarkan bantuan langsung tanpa menunggu diminta. Jangan \'Let me to help you\' — setelah \'let me\' tanpa \'to\'.',
    'Casual/neutral. Offers help directly without waiting to be asked. No \'to\' after \'let me\'.',
  ),
  'Let me get that for you': VocabUsage(
    'Your hands are full. Let me get that for you.',
    '',
    'Tanganmu penuh. Biar aku yang ambilkan.',
    '',
    'Sopan. Menawarkan mengambilkan, membukakan pintu, atau membayar (mis. kopi). \'Get\' di sini fleksibel: ambil/bawa/bayar.',
    'Polite. Offers to fetch, carry, open a door or pay for something (e.g. a coffee). \'Get\' is flexible here.',
  ),
  'Allow me': VocabUsage(
    'Allow me — I\'ll open the door for you.',
    '',
    'Mari, saya saja — saya bukakan pintunya.',
    '',
    'Sopan/formal. Menawarkan melakukan hal kecil untuk orang lain (pintu, kursi, barang jatuh). Terdengar agak resmi dan sopan.',
    'Polite/formal. Offers to do a small task for someone (a door, a chair, something dropped). Sounds courteous and a bit formal.',
  ),
  'Leave it to me': VocabUsage(
    'Don\'t worry about booking the restaurant. Leave it to me.',
    '',
    'Jangan khawatir soal pesan restoran. Serahkan padaku.',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Mengambil tanggung jawab atas suatu tugas. Variasi: \'I\'ll take care of it\', \'I\'m on it\' (kerja, santai).',
    'Casual/neutral. Takes responsibility for a task. Variants: \'I\'ll take care of it\', \'I\'m on it\' (work, casual).',
  ),
  'I\'ll see what I can do': VocabUsage(
    'The flight is full, but I\'ll see what I can do.',
    '',
    'Penerbangannya penuh, tapi akan saya usahakan.',
    '',
    'Netral. Berjanji berusaha tanpa menjamin hasil; sering dipakai petugas layanan. Jangan diartikan sebagai \'ya, pasti\'.',
    'Neutral. Promises to try without guaranteeing a result; common in customer service. Don\'t take it as a definite yes.',
  ),
  'I\'d be happy to help': VocabUsage(
    '"Could you show me how to use this machine?" "I\'d be happy to help."',
    '',
    '"Bisa tunjukkan cara memakai mesin ini?" "Dengan senang hati."',
    '',
    'Sopan. Menyanggupi permintaan dengan ramah; umum di tempat kerja dan email. Variasi: \'Happy to help!\'',
    'Polite. Accepts a request warmly; common at work and in emails. Variant: \'Happy to help!\'',
  ),
  'Help yourself': VocabUsage(
    'There\'s juice in the fridge, so help yourself.',
    '',
    'Ada jus di kulkas, silakan ambil sendiri.',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Tuan rumah mempersilakan tamu mengambil makanan/minuman sendiri. Bukan \'tolong dirimu sendiri\'. Pola: help yourself to + benda.',
    'Casual/neutral. A host invites guests to take food or drinks freely. Pattern: help yourself to + noun.',
  ),
  'I can manage': VocabUsage(
    'Thanks, but I can manage. It\'s not that heavy.',
    '',
    'Makasih, tapi aku bisa sendiri kok. Tidak terlalu berat.',
    '',
    'Netral. Menolak bantuan dengan halus; tambahkan \'Thanks, but...\' supaya tidak terdengar ketus.',
    'Neutral. Politely declines help; add \'Thanks, but...\' so it doesn\'t sound abrupt.',
  ),
  'I\'ve got it': VocabUsage(
    '"Do you want me to carry that?" "No, it\'s fine, I\'ve got it."',
    '',
    '"Mau aku bawakan?" "Nggak usah, biar aku saja."',
    '',
    'Santai. Menolak bantuan karena sudah bisa menangani; juga berarti \'aku yang bayar\' (I\'ve got this / I got it). Bisa juga berarti \'aku paham\'.',
    'Casual. Declines help because you can handle it; also used for \'I\'ll pay\'. In other contexts it can mean \'I understand\'.',
  ),
  'I\'m so sorry': VocabUsage(
    'I\'m so sorry, I forgot your birthday!',
    '',
    'Aku sungguh minta maaf, aku lupa ulang tahunmu!',
    '',
    'Netral. Permintaan maaf yang tulus. Pola: I\'m so sorry for + V-ing / about + benda. Jangan \'I\'m so sorry for forget\'.',
    'Neutral. A sincere apology. Pattern: I\'m so sorry for + V-ing / about + noun.',
  ),
  'I apologize': VocabUsage(
    'I apologize for the delay in replying to your email.',
    '',
    'Saya mohon maaf atas keterlambatan membalas email Anda.',
    '',
    'Sopan/formal. Untuk kerja, layanan pelanggan, dan email. Pola: apologize for + benda/V-ing; apologize TO seseorang. Ejaan British: apologise.',
    'Polite/formal. For work, customer service and emails. Pattern: apologize for + noun/V-ing; apologize TO someone. British: apologise.',
  ),
  'My bad': VocabUsage(
    'Oh, my bad, I thought this seat was free.',
    '',
    'Oh, salahku, kukira kursi ini kosong.',
    '',
    'Santai sekali. Hanya untuk kesalahan kecil dengan teman. Jangan dipakai ke atasan atau untuk kesalahan serius — terdengar meremehkan.',
    'Very casual. Only for small mistakes among friends. Don\'t use it with a boss or for serious mistakes; it sounds flippant.',
  ),
  'It\'s my fault': VocabUsage(
    'Don\'t blame her — it\'s my fault we missed the bus.',
    '',
    'Jangan salahkan dia — ini salahku kita ketinggalan bus.',
    '',
    'Netral. Mengaku bertanggung jawab. Variasi: \'It was my fault\'. Jangan \'It\'s my false\' — \'fault\' (kesalahan) beda dengan \'false\' (palsu/salah).',
    'Neutral. Takes responsibility. Variant: \'It was my fault\'. Don\'t confuse \'fault\' (blame) with \'false\' (not true).',
  ),
  'Sorry I\'m late': VocabUsage(
    'Sorry I\'m late — the traffic was terrible.',
    '',
    'Maaf aku terlambat — macetnya parah.',
    '',
    'Netral. Diucapkan saat baru tiba. Kalau minta maaf sebelumnya (lewat chat), bilang \'Sorry, I\'m going to be late\' atau \'I\'m running late\'.',
    'Neutral. Said on arrival. To warn in advance (e.g. by text), say \'Sorry, I\'m going to be late\' or \'I\'m running late\'.',
  ),
  'I didn\'t mean to': VocabUsage(
    'I\'m sorry I stepped on your foot. I didn\'t mean to.',
    '',
    'Maaf aku menginjak kakimu. Aku tidak sengaja.',
    '',
    'Netral. Menegaskan bahwa kesalahan tidak disengaja. Bentuk lengkap: I didn\'t mean to + verb (I didn\'t mean to hurt you).',
    'Neutral. Stresses the mistake was unintentional. Full form: I didn\'t mean to + verb (I didn\'t mean to hurt you).',
  ),
  'It won\'t happen again': VocabUsage(
    'I\'m sorry I missed the meeting. It won\'t happen again.',
    '',
    'Maaf saya tidak hadir di rapat. Tidak akan terulang lagi.',
    '',
    'Netral/sopan. Janji setelah minta maaf, umum di tempat kerja. \'Won\'t\' diucapkan wount, beda dengan \'want\' (wont).',
    'Neutral/polite. A promise after an apology, common at work. \'Won\'t\' rhymes with \'don\'t\', unlike \'want\'.',
  ),
  'Sorry for the trouble': VocabUsage(
    'Thanks for driving me home, and sorry for the trouble.',
    '',
    'Makasih sudah mengantarku pulang, dan maaf sudah merepotkan.',
    '',
    'Netral/sopan. Mirip \'maaf merepotkan\' dalam budaya Indonesia, tapi penutur asli lebih sering cukup berterima kasih. Variasi formal: \'Sorry for the inconvenience\'.',
    'Neutral/polite. Native speakers often just say thank you instead. Formal variant: \'Sorry for the inconvenience\'.',
  ),
  'No worries': VocabUsage(
    '"Sorry, I ate the last cookie." "No worries!"',
    '',
    '"Maaf, aku makan kue terakhir." "Santai aja!"',
    '',
    'Santai. Membalas maaf atau terima kasih; sangat umum di Australia dan Inggris. Jangan dipakai di situasi formal.',
    'Casual. Replies to sorry or thank you; very common in Australia and the UK. Avoid it in formal situations.',
  ),
  'Never mind': VocabUsage(
    'Never mind, I found my keys — they were in my bag.',
    '',
    'Sudahlah, kuncinya sudah ketemu — ada di tasku.',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Artinya \'lupakan, tidak penting lagi\'. Bukan balasan untuk \'thank you\'; untuk itu pakai \'You\'re welcome\' atau \'No problem\'.',
    'Casual/neutral. Means \'forget it, it doesn\'t matter now\'. Don\'t use it to answer \'thank you\' — say \'You\'re welcome\'.',
  ),
  'Don\'t worry about it': VocabUsage(
    '"I\'m sorry I broke your mug." "Don\'t worry about it, it was old anyway."',
    '',
    '"Maaf aku memecahkan cangkirmu." "Jangan dipikirkan, toh sudah tua."',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Menenangkan orang yang minta maaf. Juga bisa membalas terima kasih kecil.',
    'Casual/neutral. Reassures someone who apologizes. Can also answer a small thank you.',
  ),
  'No harm done': VocabUsage(
    '"Sorry, I bumped your car door!" "It\'s fine, no harm done."',
    '',
    '"Maaf, aku menyenggol pintu mobilmu!" "Tidak apa-apa, tidak ada yang rusak."',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Membalas maaf saat tidak ada kerugian nyata. Jangan dipakai kalau memang ada yang rusak — terdengar aneh.',
    'Casual/neutral. Replies to an apology when nothing was really damaged. Odd to say if something actually broke.',
  ),
  'Thank you so much': VocabUsage(
    'Thank you so much for helping me move house!',
    '',
    'Terima kasih banyak sudah membantuku pindahan!',
    '',
    'Netral. Terima kasih yang kuat. Pola: thank you for + benda/V-ing. Jangan \'Thank you very much for help me\' — pakai V-ing: helping.',
    'Neutral. Strong thanks. Pattern: thank you for + noun/V-ing, e.g. for helping (not \'for help me\').',
  ),
  'I owe you one': VocabUsage(
    'Thanks for covering my shift. I owe you one!',
    '',
    'Makasih sudah menggantikan shiftku. Aku utang budi sama kamu!',
    '',
    'Santai. Berterima kasih sambil berjanji membalas budi suatu hari. Hanya ke teman atau rekan dekat.',
    'Casual. Thanks someone and promises to return the favour. Use with friends or close colleagues.',
  ),
  'That\'s very kind of you': VocabUsage(
    'You brought me soup when I was sick? That\'s very kind of you.',
    '',
    'Kamu bawakan aku sup waktu aku sakit? Kamu baik sekali.',
    '',
    'Sopan. Berterima kasih atas kebaikan atau tawaran. Pakai \'of you\', bukan \'for you\'. Variasi: \'How kind of you\'.',
    'Polite. Thanks someone for a kindness or offer. Use \'of you\', not \'for you\'. Variant: \'How kind of you\'.',
  ),
  'You\'re welcome': VocabUsage(
    '"Thanks for the ride." "You\'re welcome."',
    '',
    '"Makasih tumpangannya." "Sama-sama."',
    '',
    'Netral. Balasan standar untuk \'thank you\'. Jangan tertukar dengan \'Welcome!\' saja, yang berarti \'selamat datang\'.',
    'Neutral. The standard reply to \'thank you\'. Don\'t confuse it with plain \'Welcome!\', which greets someone arriving.',
  ),
  'No problem': VocabUsage(
    '"Thanks for lending me your pen." "No problem."',
    '',
    '"Makasih sudah pinjamkan pulpenmu." "Tidak masalah."',
    '',
    'Santai. Balasan terima kasih yang paling umum di percakapan sehari-hari. Untuk tamu atau pelanggan, \'My pleasure\' terdengar lebih sopan.',
    'Casual. The most common reply to thanks in everyday speech. With guests or customers, \'My pleasure\' sounds more polite.',
  ),
  'Anytime': VocabUsage(
    '"Thanks for listening to me." "Anytime."',
    '',
    '"Makasih sudah mau mendengarkanku." "Kapan saja."',
    '',
    'Santai. Membalas terima kasih sambil menyatakan siap membantu lagi. Ditulis satu kata: anytime.',
    'Casual. Replies to thanks and says you\'d gladly help again. Written as one word: anytime.',
  ),
  'My pleasure': VocabUsage(
    '"Thank you for the lovely dinner." "My pleasure."',
    '',
    '"Terima kasih untuk makan malamnya yang enak." "Dengan senang hati."',
    '',
    'Sopan. Balasan terima kasih yang hangat; umum di hotel, restoran, dan tuan rumah. Juga: \'It was my pleasure\'.',
    'Polite. A warm reply to thanks; common in hotels, restaurants and from hosts. Also: \'It was my pleasure\'.',
  ),
  'Don\'t mention it': VocabUsage(
    '"Thanks for fixing my bike." "Don\'t mention it."',
    '',
    '"Makasih sudah membetulkan sepedaku." "Ah, bukan apa-apa."',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Artinya \'tidak perlu berterima kasih\', bukan \'jangan bilang siapa-siapa\'. Agak lebih jarang daripada \'No problem\'.',
    'Casual/neutral. Means \'no need to thank me\', not \'don\'t tell anyone\'. A little less common than \'No problem\'.',
  ),
  'That\'s great!': VocabUsage(
    '"I passed my driving test!" "That\'s great!"',
    '',
    '"Aku lulus ujian SIM!" "Bagus sekali!"',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Reaksi umum untuk kabar baik. Nada datar bisa terdengar sarkastis, jadi ucapkan dengan antusias.',
    'Casual/neutral. A common reaction to good news. Said flatly it can sound sarcastic, so say it with energy.',
  ),
  'Good for you!': VocabUsage(
    '"I finally quit smoking." "Good for you!"',
    '',
    '"Akhirnya aku berhenti merokok." "Selamat ya, ikut senang!"',
    '',
    'Santai. Memuji keberhasilan atau keputusan orang lain. Dengan nada sinis bisa berarti \'terserah kamu, aku tidak peduli\'.',
    'Casual. Praises someone\'s success or decision. In a sarcastic tone it can mean \'I don\'t care\'.',
  ),
  'Well done!': VocabUsage(
    'Well done! You finished the marathon!',
    '',
    'Kerja bagus! Kamu berhasil menyelesaikan maraton!',
    '',
    'Netral. Pujian atas usaha atau prestasi; umum di Inggris dan dari guru ke murid. Versi Amerika: \'Good job!\'',
    'Neutral. Praise for an effort or achievement; common in the UK and from teachers. American alternative: \'Good job!\'',
  ),
  'Congratulations!': VocabUsage(
    'Congratulations on your new job!',
    '',
    'Selamat atas pekerjaan barumu!',
    '',
    'Netral. Pakai \'s\' di akhir dan preposisi \'on\': Congratulations on your wedding. Bukan untuk ulang tahun (pakai \'Happy birthday\'). Santai: \'Congrats!\'',
    'Neutral. Always with \'s\' and \'on\': Congratulations on your wedding. Not for birthdays (\'Happy birthday\'). Casual: \'Congrats!\'',
  ),
  'I\'m so happy for you': VocabUsage(
    'You\'re getting married? I\'m so happy for you!',
    '',
    'Kamu mau menikah? Aku turut bahagia untukmu!',
    '',
    'Netral. Ikut merasakan kebahagiaan orang lain; lebih personal daripada \'Congratulations\'. \'For you\', bukan \'to you\'.',
    'Neutral. Shares someone\'s joy; more personal than \'Congratulations\'. Say \'for you\', not \'to you\'.',
  ),
  'Lucky you!': VocabUsage(
    'You\'re going to Bali for two weeks? Lucky you!',
    '',
    'Kamu ke Bali dua minggu? Beruntung banget kamu!',
    '',
    'Santai. Ada nada iri yang bercanda. Jangan dipakai untuk prestasi hasil kerja keras — terdengar seolah hanya untung.',
    'Casual. Playfully envious. Avoid it for achievements earned by hard work; it implies it was just luck.',
  ),
  'I can\'t wait!': VocabUsage(
    'We\'re going to the concert tomorrow — I can\'t wait!',
    '',
    'Besok kita nonton konser — aku sudah tidak sabar!',
    '',
    'Santai. Sangat antusias menunggu sesuatu. Pola: I can\'t wait to + verb / for + benda. Bukan berarti \'aku tidak bisa menunggu (pergi saja)\'.',
    'Casual. Very excited about something coming. Pattern: I can\'t wait to + verb / for + noun. It doesn\'t mean you\'ll refuse to wait.',
  ),
  'What a relief!': VocabUsage(
    'The doctor said it\'s nothing serious. What a relief!',
    '',
    'Dokter bilang tidak serius. Lega sekali!',
    '',
    'Netral. Diucapkan saat kekhawatiran berakhir. Pola \'What a + kata benda!\' (What a relief, What a surprise). Jangan \'How relief!\'',
    'Neutral. Said when a worry is over. Pattern \'What a + noun!\' (What a relief, What a surprise). Not \'How relief!\'',
  ),
  'Thank goodness': VocabUsage(
    'Thank goodness you\'re here — I was getting worried.',
    '',
    'Syukurlah kamu di sini — aku mulai khawatir.',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Lega karena hal buruk tidak terjadi. Variasi: \'Thank God\' (lebih umum, tapi sebagian orang menghindarinya).',
    'Casual/neutral. Relief that something bad didn\'t happen. Variant: \'Thank God\' (more common, though some people avoid it).',
  ),
  'Really?': VocabUsage(
    '"I\'ve been to twenty countries." "Really? That\'s amazing!"',
    '',
    '"Aku sudah ke dua puluh negara." "Masa sih? Keren!"',
    '',
    'Santai. Menunjukkan tertarik atau sedikit kaget, bukan menuduh bohong. Nada naik = tertarik; nada datar bisa terdengar tidak percaya.',
    'Casual. Shows interest or mild surprise, not an accusation of lying. Rising tone = interested; flat tone can sound doubtful.',
  ),
  'No way!': VocabUsage(
    '"I won the lottery!" "No way!"',
    '',
    '"Aku menang lotre!" "Masa?! Nggak mungkin!"',
    '',
    'Santai. Kaget atau tidak percaya (biasanya kabar baik). Bisa juga berarti penolakan keras: \'No way, I\'m not doing that.\'',
    'Casual. Surprise or disbelief (often at good news). Can also be a strong refusal: \'No way, I\'m not doing that.\'',
  ),
  'You\'re kidding!': VocabUsage(
    'You\'re kidding! You met the president?',
    '',
    'Kamu bercanda, kan! Kamu ketemu presiden?',
    '',
    'Santai. Kaget mendengar kabar yang sulit dipercaya. Variasi: \'You\'re joking!\', \'Are you kidding me?\' (bisa terdengar kesal).',
    'Casual. Surprise at hard-to-believe news. Variants: \'You\'re joking!\', \'Are you kidding me?\' (can sound annoyed).',
  ),
  'I can\'t believe it': VocabUsage(
    'We won the final! I can\'t believe it!',
    '',
    'Kita menang di final! Aku tidak percaya!',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa untuk kabar baik maupun buruk; nada menentukan. Pola: I can\'t believe + kalimat (I can\'t believe you did that).',
    'Neutral. Works for good or bad news; tone decides. Pattern: I can\'t believe + clause (I can\'t believe you did that).',
  ),
  'Oh no!': VocabUsage(
    'Oh no! I left my phone on the bus.',
    '',
    'Aduh! Ponselku ketinggalan di bus.',
    '',
    'Santai. Reaksi spontan terhadap masalah atau kabar buruk. Untuk kabar duka, lanjutkan dengan \'I\'m so sorry\'.',
    'Casual. A spontaneous reaction to a problem or bad news. For sad news, follow it with \'I\'m so sorry\'.',
  ),
  'That\'s too bad': VocabUsage(
    '"The concert was cancelled." "That\'s too bad."',
    '',
    '"Konsernya dibatalkan." "Sayang sekali."',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Simpati untuk kekecewaan kecil. Untuk kabar serius (sakit, meninggal) terlalu ringan — pakai \'I\'m sorry to hear that\'.',
    'Casual/neutral. Sympathy for small disappointments. Too light for serious news like illness or death — use \'I\'m sorry to hear that\'.',
  ),
  'What a shame': VocabUsage(
    'You can\'t come to the wedding? What a shame.',
    '',
    'Kamu tidak bisa datang ke pernikahan? Sayang banget, ya.',
    '',
    'Netral. Menyesali situasi yang disayangkan. \'Shame\' di sini bukan \'malu\'. Variasi: \'What a pity\', \'It\'s a shame that...\'',
    'Neutral. Regrets an unfortunate situation. \'Shame\' here doesn\'t mean embarrassment. Variants: \'What a pity\', \'It\'s a shame that...\'',
  ),
  'I\'m sorry to hear that': VocabUsage(
    '"My grandfather passed away last week." "I\'m sorry to hear that."',
    '',
    '"Kakekku meninggal minggu lalu." "Aku ikut prihatin."',
    '',
    'Netral/sopan. Simpati untuk kabar buruk; di sini \'sorry\' bukan minta maaf. Aman dipakai di situasi apa pun, termasuk kerja.',
    'Neutral/polite. Sympathy for bad news; \'sorry\' here isn\'t an apology. Safe in any situation, including work.',
  ),
  'How awful!': VocabUsage(
    'They lost everything in the flood? How awful!',
    '',
    'Mereka kehilangan segalanya karena banjir? Mengerikan sekali!',
    '',
    'Netral. Reaksi kuat untuk kabar sangat buruk. Pola \'How + kata sifat!\' (How awful, How sad). Jangan \'What awful!\'',
    'Neutral. A strong reaction to very bad news. Pattern \'How + adjective!\' (How awful, How sad). Not \'What awful!\'',
  ),
  'I\'m sick of it': VocabUsage(
    'It\'s been raining for two weeks. I\'m sick of it!',
    '',
    'Sudah hujan dua minggu. Aku sudah muak!',
    '',
    'Santai. Bosan dan kesal karena sesuatu terus terjadi; bukan berarti sakit. Pola: I\'m sick of + benda/V-ing. Variasi: \'I\'m tired of it\'.',
    'Casual. Fed up because something keeps happening; it doesn\'t mean ill. Pattern: I\'m sick of + noun/V-ing. Variant: \'I\'m tired of it\'.',
  ),
  'That\'s so annoying': VocabUsage(
    'My neighbour plays loud music every night. That\'s so annoying.',
    '',
    'Tetanggaku setel musik keras tiap malam. Nyebelin banget.',
    '',
    'Santai. Mengungkapkan kesal pada situasi atau kebiasaan. \'Annoying\' = menyebalkan (penyebab); \'annoyed\' = merasa kesal (orangnya): I\'m annoyed.',
    'Casual. Expresses irritation at a situation. \'Annoying\' describes the cause; \'annoyed\' describes how you feel: I\'m annoyed.',
  ),
  'Long time no see': VocabUsage(
    'Hey, Sarah! Long time no see. How have you been?',
    '',
    'Hai, Sarah! Lama tidak bertemu. Apa kabarmu selama ini?',
    '',
    'Santai. Untuk teman/kenalan yang lama tak dijumpai. Jawaban umum: \'Yeah, it\'s been ages!\'',
    'Casual. For friends you haven\'t seen in a while. Common reply: \'Yeah, it\'s been ages!\'',
  ),
  'How\'s it going?': VocabUsage(
    'Hi, Tom! How\'s it going? - Not bad, thanks. You?',
    '',
    'Hai, Tom! Gimana kabarnya? - Lumayan, makasih. Kamu?',
    '',
    'Santai. Sapaan, bukan pertanyaan serius. Jawab singkat: \'Good, you?\' atau \'Not bad.\' Jangan dijawab \'It\'s going to...\'.',
    'Casual. A greeting, not a real question. Reply briefly: \'Good, you?\' or \'Not bad.\'',
  ),
  'What\'s up?': VocabUsage(
    'What\'s up, man? - Not much, just chilling.',
    '',
    'Ada apa, bro? - Nggak ada apa-apa, lagi santai aja.',
    '',
    'Santai sekali, antarteman. Jawaban umum: \'Not much.\' / \'Nothing much.\' Jangan dijawab \'The sky\' atau \'I\'m fine\' secara kaku; hindari ke atasan.',
    'Very casual, among friends. Common reply: \'Not much.\' Avoid with bosses or strangers.',
  ),
  'How have you been?': VocabUsage(
    'It\'s great to see you again! How have you been?',
    '',
    'Senang bertemu lagi! Apa kabarmu selama ini?',
    '',
    'Netral. Dipakai setelah lama tak bertemu, bukan untuk orang yang kemarin baru ditemui. Jawaban: \'I\'ve been good, thanks.\'',
    'Neutral. Used after not seeing someone for a while. Reply: \'I\'ve been good, thanks.\'',
  ),
  'Nice to meet you': VocabUsage(
    'Hi, I\'m Dani. - Hi Dani, I\'m Lisa. Nice to meet you.',
    '',
    'Hai, saya Dani. - Hai Dani, saya Lisa. Senang berkenalan.',
    '',
    'Netral. Hanya saat pertama kali berkenalan. Balasan: \'Nice to meet you too.\' Saat berpisah: \'Nice meeting you.\'',
    'Neutral. Only on first meeting. Reply: \'Nice to meet you too.\' When leaving: \'Nice meeting you.\'',
  ),
  'What do you do?': VocabUsage(
    'So, what do you do? - I\'m a nurse at the city hospital.',
    '',
    'Jadi, kamu kerja apa? - Saya perawat di rumah sakit kota.',
    '',
    'Netral. Artinya \'apa pekerjaanmu\', bukan \'sedang apa\'. Untuk \'sedang apa\' pakai \'What are you doing?\'.',
    'Neutral. Means \'what\'s your job\', not \'what are you doing right now\'.',
  ),
  'Where are you from?': VocabUsage(
    'Your English is great. Where are you from? - I\'m from Bandung.',
    '',
    'Bahasa Inggrismu bagus. Kamu dari mana? - Saya dari Bandung.',
    '',
    'Netral. Menanyakan asal kota/negara. Jawab \'I\'m from...\' tanpa \'I come from\' yang terdengar kaku. Jangan lupa \'from\' di akhir.',
    'Neutral. Asks about hometown/country. Reply \'I\'m from...\'. Don\'t drop the final \'from\'.',
  ),
  'How\'s your day going?': VocabUsage(
    'Morning, Jake! How\'s your day going so far?',
    '',
    'Pagi, Jake! Bagaimana harimu sejauh ini?',
    '',
    'Netral. Sapaan ramah di kantor atau kasir. Jawab singkat: \'Pretty good, thanks. Yours?\'',
    'Neutral. Friendly greeting at work or a checkout. Reply briefly: \'Pretty good, thanks. Yours?\'',
  ),
  'Lovely weather, isn\'t it?': VocabUsage(
    'Lovely weather, isn\'t it? Perfect day for a walk.',
    '',
    'Cuacanya cerah, ya? Pas buat jalan-jalan.',
    '',
    'Netral, sangat British. Pembuka basa-basi dengan orang asing. Cukup setuju ringan: \'Yes, beautiful!\'',
    'Neutral, very British. Small-talk opener with strangers. Just agree lightly: \'Yes, beautiful!\'',
  ),
  'Have we met before?': VocabUsage(
    'Sorry, have we met before? You look really familiar.',
    '',
    'Maaf, apa kita pernah bertemu sebelumnya? Wajahmu terasa familier.',
    '',
    'Netral. Saat merasa kenal wajah seseorang. Awali dengan \'Sorry\' atau \'Excuse me\' agar sopan.',
    'Neutral. When someone looks familiar. Start with \'Sorry\' or \'Excuse me\' to sound polite.',
  ),
  'I don\'t think we\'ve met': VocabUsage(
    'Hi, I don\'t think we\'ve met. I\'m Rina from marketing.',
    '',
    'Hai, sepertinya kita belum berkenalan. Saya Rina dari bagian pemasaran.',
    '',
    'Sopan/formal. Cara halus memperkenalkan diri di acara atau kantor. Langsung lanjutkan dengan nama Anda.',
    'Polite/formal. A smooth way to introduce yourself at events or work. Follow with your name.',
  ),
  'Mind if I join you?': VocabUsage(
    'Mind if I join you? All the other tables are full.',
    '',
    'Boleh saya bergabung? Meja lain penuh semua.',
    '',
    'Netral. Jawaban \'No\' berarti BOLEH (\'No, not at all\'). Jebakan: jangan jawab \'Yes\' kalau maksudnya mengizinkan.',
    'Neutral. Answer \'No, not at all\' to mean yes. Trap: \'Yes\' would mean you DO mind.',
  ),
  'What brings you here?': VocabUsage(
    'What brings you here? Are you on holiday or working?',
    '',
    'Apa yang membawamu ke sini? Sedang liburan atau kerja?',
    '',
    'Netral. Menanyakan alasan datang ke tempat/acara/kota. Lebih ramah daripada \'Why are you here?\' yang terdengar curiga.',
    'Neutral. Asks why someone came. Friendlier than \'Why are you here?\', which sounds suspicious.',
  ),
  'How do you know each other?': VocabUsage(
    'You two seem close. How do you know each other?',
    '',
    'Kalian kelihatan akrab. Bagaimana kalian bisa saling kenal?',
    '',
    'Netral. Pembuka obrolan di pesta. Versi tunggal: \'How do you know Anna?\' (kenal tuan rumah dari mana).',
    'Neutral. Party conversation starter. Singular version: \'How do you know Anna?\'',
  ),
  'What\'s new?': VocabUsage(
    'Hey, what\'s new? Did you finally move house?',
    '',
    'Hei, ada kabar terbaru apa? Jadi pindah rumah akhirnya?',
    '',
    'Santai. Sapaan antarteman. Jawaban umum: \'Not much.\' / \'Same old, same old.\'',
    'Casual. Greeting among friends. Common reply: \'Not much.\' / \'Same old, same old.\'',
  ),
  'How was your weekend?': VocabUsage(
    'How was your weekend? Did you do anything fun?',
    '',
    'Bagaimana akhir pekanmu? Ada kegiatan seru?',
    '',
    'Netral. Basa-basi khas hari Senin di kantor. Pakai \'was\' (lampau), bukan \'is\'.',
    'Neutral. Typical Monday small talk at work. Use past \'was\', not \'is\'.',
  ),
  'Any plans for the weekend?': VocabUsage(
    'It\'s finally Friday! Any plans for the weekend?',
    '',
    'Akhirnya Jumat! Ada rencana akhir pekan ini?',
    '',
    'Santai. Basa-basi menjelang akhir pekan. Orang Inggris bilang \'at the weekend\', Amerika \'on the weekend\'.',
    'Casual. Small talk before the weekend. UK says \'at the weekend\', US \'on the weekend\'.',
  ),
  'Is this seat taken?': VocabUsage(
    'Excuse me, is this seat taken? - No, go ahead.',
    '',
    'Permisi, kursi ini ada yang menempati? - Tidak, silakan.',
    '',
    'Netral. Di kafe, bus, atau acara. Jawaban \'No\' berarti kursinya kosong dan boleh dipakai.',
    'Neutral. In cafes, buses or events. \'No\' means the seat is free.',
  ),
  'Good to see you': VocabUsage(
    'Ben! Good to see you. It\'s been a while.',
    '',
    'Ben! Senang bertemu lagi. Sudah lama ya.',
    '',
    'Netral. Untuk orang yang sudah dikenal. Untuk orang baru, pakai \'Nice to meet you\', bukan \'Nice to see you\'.',
    'Neutral. For people you already know. For new people use \'Nice to meet you\'.',
  ),
  'Fancy seeing you here': VocabUsage(
    'Well, fancy seeing you here! I didn\'t know you shopped here too.',
    '',
    'Wah, tak disangka ketemu di sini! Saya tidak tahu kamu belanja di sini juga.',
    '',
    'Santai, terutama British. Kejutan saat bertemu kenalan secara kebetulan. \'Fancy\' di sini bukan berarti \'mewah\'.',
    'Casual, mainly British. Surprise at bumping into someone. \'Fancy\' here doesn\'t mean \'luxurious\'.',
  ),
  'How\'s work?': VocabUsage(
    'How\'s work these days? Still busy with the new project?',
    '',
    'Gimana kerjaanmu belakangan ini? Masih sibuk dengan proyek baru?',
    '',
    'Santai. Basa-basi dengan teman/keluarga. Jawaban umum: \'Busy, but good.\'',
    'Casual. Small talk with friends or family. Common reply: \'Busy, but good.\'',
  ),
  'I\'d better get going': VocabUsage(
    'Look at the time! I\'d better get going before the traffic gets bad.',
    '',
    'Lihat jamnya! Sebaiknya saya pergi sekarang sebelum macet.',
    '',
    'Netral. Sinyal halus untuk mengakhiri obrolan. Variasi: \'I should get going.\'',
    'Neutral. A soft signal to end a conversation. Variation: \'I should get going.\'',
  ),
  'It was nice talking to you': VocabUsage(
    'It was nice talking to you. Good luck with the interview!',
    '',
    'Senang mengobrol denganmu. Semoga sukses wawancaranya!',
    '',
    'Sopan/formal. Penutup obrolan dengan kenalan baru atau rekan. Balasan: \'You too!\'',
    'Polite/formal. Closing a chat with a new acquaintance or colleague. Reply: \'You too!\'',
  ),
  'Take care': VocabUsage(
    'Okay, see you next week. Take care!',
    '',
    'Oke, sampai minggu depan. Jaga dirimu baik-baik!',
    '',
    'Santai. Salam perpisahan hangat, juga di akhir pesan. Balasan: \'You too!\'',
    'Casual. Warm goodbye, also at the end of messages. Reply: \'You too!\'',
  ),
  'See you later': VocabUsage(
    'I\'m heading out now. See you later!',
    '',
    'Saya keluar dulu. Sampai jumpa nanti!',
    '',
    'Santai. Dipakai walau belum tentu bertemu hari itu juga. Bentuk pendek: \'See ya!\' / \'Later!\'',
    'Casual. Used even if you won\'t meet again that day. Short forms: \'See ya!\' / \'Later!\'',
  ),
  'See you around': VocabUsage(
    'Nice chatting with you. See you around!',
    '',
    'Senang ngobrol denganmu. Sampai ketemu lagi kapan-kapan!',
    '',
    'Santai. Tanpa janji bertemu yang pasti, misalnya dengan tetangga atau teman kampus.',
    'Casual. No fixed plan to meet, e.g. with neighbours or classmates.',
  ),
  'Catch you later': VocabUsage(
    'Gotta go, my bus is here. Catch you later!',
    '',
    'Harus pergi, busku datang. Nanti ngobrol lagi ya!',
    '',
    'Santai sekali, antarteman. Jangan dipakai ke atasan atau klien.',
    'Very casual, among friends. Don\'t use with bosses or clients.',
  ),
  'Have a good one': VocabUsage(
    'Thanks for the coffee. Have a good one!',
    '',
    'Makasih kopinya. Semoga lancar harimu!',
    '',
    'Santai, khas Amerika. Sering diucapkan ke kasir atau orang asing. Balasan: \'You too!\'',
    'Casual, typically American. Often said to cashiers or strangers. Reply: \'You too!\'',
  ),
  'Have a nice day': VocabUsage(
    'Here\'s your receipt. Have a nice day!',
    '',
    'Ini struknya. Semoga harimu menyenangkan!',
    '',
    'Netral. Ucapan standar petugas toko/layanan. Balasan: \'Thanks, you too!\' Jangan balas \'Same to you\' dengan nada kaku.',
    'Neutral. Standard phrase from shop or service staff. Reply: \'Thanks, you too!\'',
  ),
  'Keep in touch': VocabUsage(
    'Good luck in Jakarta, and keep in touch!',
    '',
    'Semoga sukses di Jakarta, dan tetap berkabar ya!',
    '',
    'Netral. Saat berpisah dengan orang yang akan jarang ditemui. Pakai \'in touch\', bukan \'in contact\' dalam ungkapan ini.',
    'Neutral. When parting from someone you\'ll rarely see. The fixed phrase is \'in touch\'.',
  ),
  'Say hi to everyone for me': VocabUsage(
    'Are you going home for Eid? Say hi to everyone for me!',
    '',
    'Kamu mudik Lebaran? Titip salam untuk semuanya ya!',
    '',
    'Santai. Versi sopan: \'Please give my regards to...\'. Pola: say hi to + orang + for me.',
    'Casual. Polite version: \'Please give my regards to...\'. Pattern: say hi to + person + for me.',
  ),
  'Let\'s catch up soon': VocabUsage(
    'I have to run, but let\'s catch up soon over coffee.',
    '',
    'Saya harus pergi, tapi kapan-kapan kita ngopi dan ngobrol lagi ya.',
    '',
    'Santai. Ajakan bertemu untuk saling bertukar kabar. Sering hanya basa-basi, belum tentu janji pasti.',
    'Casual. Suggests meeting to share news. Often just polite talk, not a firm plan.',
  ),
  'I\'ve got to run': VocabUsage(
    'Sorry, I\'ve got to run. My meeting starts in five minutes.',
    '',
    'Maaf, saya harus buru-buru pergi. Rapat saya mulai lima menit lagi.',
    '',
    'Santai. \'Run\' di sini bukan berarti berlari, tapi segera pergi. Versi lisan: \'Gotta run!\'',
    'Casual. \'Run\' means leave quickly, not literally run. Spoken form: \'Gotta run!\'',
  ),
  'Safe travels': VocabUsage(
    'Enjoy your trip to Bali. Safe travels!',
    '',
    'Selamat menikmati perjalanan ke Bali. Hati-hati di jalan!',
    '',
    'Netral. Untuk orang yang akan bepergian jauh (pesawat, kereta). Untuk pulang ke rumah, pakai \'Get home safe\'.',
    'Neutral. For someone going on a trip. For going home, use \'Get home safe\'.',
  ),
  'Get home safe': VocabUsage(
    'It\'s dark out there. Get home safe, okay?',
    '',
    'Di luar sudah gelap. Hati-hati sampai rumah, ya?',
    '',
    'Santai. Diucapkan saat teman pulang malam. Versi lain: \'Text me when you get home.\'',
    'Casual. Said when a friend leaves at night. Also: \'Text me when you get home.\'',
  ),
  'Until next time': VocabUsage(
    'Thanks for watching, everyone. Until next time!',
    '',
    'Terima kasih sudah menonton, semuanya. Sampai jumpa di lain waktu!',
    '',
    'Netral. Sering dipakai di akhir video, siaran, atau pertemuan rutin.',
    'Neutral. Common at the end of videos, broadcasts or regular meetings.',
  ),
  'Talk to you soon': VocabUsage(
    'Okay, I\'ll send you the details tonight. Talk to you soon!',
    '',
    'Oke, nanti malam saya kirim detailnya. Nanti kita bicara lagi!',
    '',
    'Santai. Penutup telepon, chat, atau email ke orang dekat. Singkatan chat: \'TTYS\'.',
    'Casual. Closing calls, chats or emails to people you know. Chat shorthand: \'TTYS\'.',
  ),
  'Don\'t be a stranger': VocabUsage(
    'It was great having you over. Don\'t be a stranger!',
    '',
    'Senang kamu sudah mampir. Sering-sering kabari ya!',
    '',
    'Santai. Bukan berarti \'jangan jadi orang asing\' secara harfiah, tapi \'sering-seringlah menghubungi/mampir\'.',
    'Casual. Not literal; it means \'stay in contact\' or \'visit again\'.',
  ),
  'It\'s getting late': VocabUsage(
    'Wow, it\'s getting late. I should head home.',
    '',
    'Wah, sudah larut nih. Saya sebaiknya pulang.',
    '',
    'Netral. Isyarat halus untuk pamit atau mengakhiri acara. Biasanya diikuti \'I should go\'.',
    'Neutral. A gentle hint to leave or wrap up. Usually followed by \'I should go\'.',
  ),
  'I\'ll let you go': VocabUsage(
    'Anyway, I\'ll let you go. Thanks for calling!',
    '',
    'Ya sudah, saya tidak mau menahanmu lagi. Makasih sudah menelepon!',
    '',
    'Netral. Cara sopan menutup telepon tanpa terkesan ingin cepat selesai. Bukan berarti \'saya melepaskanmu\'.',
    'Neutral. Polite way to end a call without sounding eager to hang up.',
  ),
  'Bye for now': VocabUsage(
    'That\'s all from me today. Bye for now!',
    '',
    'Itu saja dari saya hari ini. Dadah, sampai nanti!',
    '',
    'Santai. Pamit ringan yang menyiratkan akan berhubungan lagi, cocok di telepon atau pesan.',
    'Casual. Light goodbye implying more contact soon; good for calls or messages.',
  ),
  'Could you say that again?': VocabUsage(
    'Sorry, could you say that again? It\'s a bit noisy here.',
    '',
    'Maaf, bisa diulangi? Di sini agak berisik.',
    '',
    'Sopan/formal. Awali dengan \'Sorry\'. Hindari \'Repeat!\' saja karena terdengar seperti perintah.',
    'Polite/formal. Start with \'Sorry\'. Avoid just \'Repeat!\', which sounds like an order.',
  ),
  'Pardon?': VocabUsage(
    'Pardon? I didn\'t hear the last part.',
    '',
    'Maaf, apa tadi? Saya tidak dengar bagian akhirnya.',
    '',
    'Sopan/formal. Diucapkan dengan nada naik. Amerika lebih sering \'Sorry?\' atau \'Excuse me?\'. Jangan menjawab \'What?\' saja, terdengar kasar.',
    'Polite/formal. Said with rising tone. Americans often say \'Sorry?\'. A bare \'What?\' can sound rude.',
  ),
  'Come again?': VocabUsage(
    'Come again? You\'re moving to Canada?',
    '',
    'Hah, apa tadi? Kamu mau pindah ke Kanada?',
    '',
    'Santai. Sering menunjukkan kaget atau tidak percaya. Jangan dipakai ke atasan; pakai \'Pardon?\'.',
    'Casual. Often shows surprise or disbelief. With bosses, use \'Pardon?\' instead.',
  ),
  'I didn\'t catch that': VocabUsage(
    'Sorry, I didn\'t catch that. What was your name again?',
    '',
    'Maaf, saya kurang menangkap. Siapa namamu tadi?',
    '',
    'Netral. \'Catch\' di sini artinya mendengar/menangkap ucapan. Lebih halus daripada \'I don\'t understand\'.',
    'Neutral. \'Catch\' means hear. Softer than \'I don\'t understand\'.',
  ),
  'What do you mean?': VocabUsage(
    'What do you mean the meeting is cancelled? Nobody told me.',
    '',
    'Apa maksudmu rapatnya dibatalkan? Tidak ada yang memberi tahu saya.',
    '',
    'Netral. Nada tinggi bisa terdengar menantang; lembutkan dengan \'Sorry, what do you mean by...?\'. Jangan bilang \'What is your mean?\'.',
    'Neutral. A sharp tone can sound challenging; soften with \'Sorry, what do you mean by...?\'',
  ),
  'Could you speak a bit slower?': VocabUsage(
    'Could you speak a bit slower? My English isn\'t very good yet.',
    '',
    'Bisa bicara sedikit lebih pelan? Bahasa Inggris saya belum terlalu bagus.',
    '',
    'Sopan/formal. Tambahkan \'please\' agar lebih halus. Pakai \'slower\' atau \'more slowly\', bukan \'more slower\'.',
    'Polite/formal. Add \'please\' to soften. Use \'slower\' or \'more slowly\', not \'more slower\'.',
  ),
  'How do you spell that?': VocabUsage(
    'Your last name is Wijaya? How do you spell that?',
    '',
    'Nama belakangmu Wijaya? Bagaimana ejaannya?',
    '',
    'Netral. Penting saat telepon atau mengisi formulir. Jangan \'How to spell?\' tanpa subjek.',
    'Neutral. Useful on the phone or with forms. Don\'t say \'How to spell?\' without a subject.',
  ),
  'Does that make sense?': VocabUsage(
    'So we pay first and claim it back later. Does that make sense?',
    '',
    'Jadi kita bayar dulu lalu klaim belakangan. Penjelasan saya bisa dipahami?',
    '',
    'Netral. Mengecek pemahaman pendengar tanpa terkesan meremehkan. Lebih sopan daripada \'Do you understand?\'.',
    'Neutral. Checks understanding without sounding condescending. Politer than \'Do you understand?\'',
  ),
  'You know what I mean?': VocabUsage(
    'It\'s not bad, it\'s just... different. You know what I mean?',
    '',
    'Bukan jelek, cuma... beda aja. Kamu paham maksudku kan?',
    '',
    'Santai. Sering diucapkan cepat \'Know what I mean?\'. Jangan dipakai berlebihan, terdengar seperti kebiasaan.',
    'Casual. Often shortened to \'Know what I mean?\'. Overusing it sounds like a verbal tic.',
  ),
  'So what you\'re saying is': VocabUsage(
    'So what you\'re saying is we need two more weeks?',
    '',
    'Jadi maksudmu, kita butuh dua minggu lagi?',
    '',
    'Netral. Mengulang dengan kata sendiri untuk memastikan paham. Nada datar agar tidak terdengar menyindir.',
    'Neutral. Paraphrases to confirm understanding. Keep a neutral tone so it doesn\'t sound sarcastic.',
  ),
  'Let me see': VocabUsage(
    'Let me see... the next train leaves at 4:15.',
    '',
    'Coba saya lihat dulu... kereta berikutnya berangkat jam 4.15.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pengisi jeda saat berpikir atau mencari informasi. Juga \'Let\'s see.\'',
    'Neutral. Filler while thinking or checking information. Also \'Let\'s see.\'',
  ),
  'Let me think': VocabUsage(
    'Which one is better? Hmm, let me think.',
    '',
    'Mana yang lebih baik? Hmm, biar saya pikir dulu.',
    '',
    'Netral. Meminta waktu berpikir sebelum menjawab. Variasi: \'Let me think about it.\'',
    'Neutral. Asks for time before answering. Variation: \'Let me think about it.\'',
  ),
  'Good question': VocabUsage(
    'Good question. I\'m not sure, but I\'ll find out for you.',
    '',
    'Pertanyaan bagus. Saya belum yakin, tapi akan saya cari tahu.',
    '',
    'Netral. Sering dipakai untuk mengulur waktu menjawab pertanyaan sulit, misalnya saat presentasi atau wawancara.',
    'Neutral. Often used to buy time before a hard question, e.g. in presentations or interviews.',
  ),
  'How can I put it?': VocabUsage(
    'He\'s... how can I put it? A little too honest.',
    '',
    'Dia itu... bagaimana ya bilangnya? Agak terlalu jujur.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pengisi saat mencari kata yang halus atau tepat. Variasi: \'How should I put this?\'',
    'Neutral. Filler while looking for a tactful or exact word. Variation: \'How should I put this?\'',
  ),
  'What\'s the word?': VocabUsage(
    'It\'s like a... what\'s the word? A shortcut.',
    '',
    'Itu semacam... apa ya istilahnya? Jalan pintas.',
    '',
    'Santai. Saat lupa sebuah kata; lawan bicara sering membantu menebak. Variasi: \'What\'s it called?\'',
    'Casual. When a word slips your mind; listeners often help. Variation: \'What\'s it called?\'',
  ),
  'You know': VocabUsage(
    'I was, you know, kind of nervous about the exam.',
    '',
    'Saya tuh, ya gitu, agak gugup soal ujiannya.',
    '',
    'Santai. Pengisi jeda, bukan pertanyaan. Jangan dipakai terlalu sering atau dalam situasi formal.',
    'Casual. A filler, not a question. Don\'t overuse it or use it in formal settings.',
  ),
  'I mean': VocabUsage(
    'The food was okay. I mean, it wasn\'t great, but it was fine.',
    '',
    'Makanannya lumayan. Maksud saya, tidak istimewa, tapi oke.',
    '',
    'Santai. Untuk memperbaiki atau memperjelas ucapan sendiri. Bukan untuk bertanya maksud orang lain.',
    'Casual. Corrects or clarifies what you just said. Not for asking what others mean.',
  ),
  'Where was I?': VocabUsage(
    'Sorry about that phone call. Now, where was I?',
    '',
    'Maaf soal telepon tadi. Nah, tadi sampai mana ya?',
    '',
    'Netral. Setelah diinterupsi dan lupa sampai mana bicara. Lawan bicara bisa membantu: \'You were talking about...\'',
    'Neutral. After an interruption. The listener can help: \'You were talking about...\'',
  ),
  'As I was saying': VocabUsage(
    'As I was saying, the deadline is next Friday.',
    '',
    'Seperti yang tadi saya bilang, tenggatnya Jumat depan.',
    '',
    'Netral. Kembali ke topik setelah terpotong. Nada tegas bisa terdengar menegur orang yang memotong.',
    'Neutral. Returns to your point after an interruption. A firm tone can sound like a rebuke.',
  ),
  'Hold on a sec': VocabUsage(
    'Hold on a sec, I need to grab my keys.',
    '',
    'Tunggu sebentar, saya ambil kunci dulu.',
    '',
    'Santai. \'Sec\' singkatan dari \'second\'. Versi sopan: \'Just a moment, please.\'',
    'Casual. \'Sec\' is short for \'second\'. Polite version: \'Just a moment, please.\'',
  ),
  'Just looking, thanks': VocabUsage(
    'Can I help you find anything? - Just looking, thanks.',
    '',
    'Ada yang bisa saya bantu? - Cuma lihat-lihat, terima kasih.',
    '',
    'Netral. Jawaban sopan ke pramuniaga. Lebih wajar daripada \'No\' saja yang terdengar ketus.',
    'Neutral. Polite reply to shop staff. More natural than a bare \'No\'.',
  ),
  'How much is this?': VocabUsage(
    'Excuse me, how much is this? I can\'t find the price tag.',
    '',
    'Permisi, ini berapa harganya? Saya tidak menemukan label harganya.',
    '',
    'Netral. Jamak: \'How much are these?\'. Jangan \'How much the price?\'.',
    'Neutral. Plural: \'How much are these?\'. Avoid \'How much the price?\'',
  ),
  'Do you have this in another size?': VocabUsage(
    'This is too tight. Do you have this in another size?',
    '',
    'Ini terlalu sempit. Ada ukuran lain untuk yang ini?',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa lebih spesifik: \'in a medium\', \'in a bigger size\', \'in blue\'. Perhatikan preposisi \'in\'.',
    'Neutral. Be specific: \'in a medium\', \'in a bigger size\', \'in blue\'. Note the preposition \'in\'.',
  ),
  'Can I try this on?': VocabUsage(
    'I like this jacket. Can I try this on?',
    '',
    'Saya suka jaket ini. Boleh saya coba pakai?',
    '',
    'Netral. Untuk pakaian/sepatu pakai \'try on\'; untuk makanan pakai \'try\' saja. Jangan \'try this on\' untuk mencicipi.',
    'Neutral. \'Try on\' is for clothes/shoes; for food just \'try\'.',
  ),
  'Where\'s the fitting room?': VocabUsage(
    'Excuse me, where\'s the fitting room? - It\'s at the back, on the left.',
    '',
    'Permisi, kamar pasnya di mana? - Di belakang, sebelah kiri.',
    '',
    'Netral. Amerika juga menyebut \'dressing room\' atau \'changing room\'.',
    'Neutral. Also called \'dressing room\' or \'changing room\'.',
  ),
  'Is this on sale?': VocabUsage(
    'Is this on sale? The sign says 30% off.',
    '',
    'Ini sedang diskon? Tandanya bilang potongan 30%.',
    '',
    'Netral. Jebakan: \'on sale\' biasanya berarti \'sedang diskon\', sedangkan \'for sale\' berarti \'dijual\'.',
    'Neutral. Trap: \'on sale\' usually means discounted, while \'for sale\' means available to buy.',
  ),
  'Do you take cards?': VocabUsage(
    'Do you take cards, or is it cash only?',
    '',
    'Bisa bayar pakai kartu, atau hanya tunai?',
    '',
    'Netral. \'Take\' di sini artinya \'menerima\'. Variasi: \'Can I pay by card?\' (pakai \'by\', bukan \'with\').',
    'Neutral. \'Take\' means accept. Variation: \'Can I pay by card?\'',
  ),
  'I\'ll take it': VocabUsage(
    'It fits perfectly. I\'ll take it!',
    '',
    'Pas sekali. Saya ambil yang ini!',
    '',
    'Netral. Artinya \'saya beli\', bukan mengambil gratis. Jamak: \'I\'ll take them.\'',
    'Neutral. Means \'I\'ll buy it\', not take it for free. Plural: \'I\'ll take them.\'',
  ),
  'Keep the change': VocabUsage(
    'Here\'s twenty dollars. Keep the change.',
    '',
    'Ini dua puluh dolar. Kembaliannya ambil saja.',
    '',
    'Santai. Cara memberi tip ke sopir taksi atau pelayan. Jangan dipakai kalau kembaliannya besar kecuali memang mau memberi.',
    'Casual. A way to tip a driver or server. Only say it if you\'re happy to leave the whole amount.',
  ),
  'Can I get a receipt?': VocabUsage(
    'Can I get a receipt, please? I need it for work.',
    '',
    'Boleh minta struknya? Saya perlu untuk kantor.',
    '',
    'Netral. Huruf \'p\' di \'receipt\' tidak dibaca: ri-sit. Versi sopan: \'Could I have a receipt?\'',
    'Neutral. The \'p\' in \'receipt\' is silent. Politer: \'Could I have a receipt?\'',
  ),
  'A table for two, please': VocabUsage(
    'Good evening. A table for two, please.',
    '',
    'Selamat malam. Meja untuk dua orang.',
    '',
    'Netral. Ucapkan ke pelayan di pintu masuk; ganti angka sesuai jumlah orang. Jangan \'Two people table\'.',
    'Neutral. Say it to the host at the door; change the number as needed.',
  ),
  'I have a reservation': VocabUsage(
    'Hi, I have a reservation under the name Putri.',
    '',
    'Halo, saya sudah reservasi atas nama Putri.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pakai \'under the name...\', bukan \'with the name\' atau \'on behalf\'. Di Inggris juga lazim \'I have a booking\'.',
    'Neutral. Use \'under the name...\'. British English also says \'I have a booking.\'',
  ),
  'Can I see the menu?': VocabUsage(
    'Hi, can I see the menu, please?',
    '',
    'Halo, boleh lihat menunya?',
    '',
    'Netral. Tambahkan \'please\'. Alternatif: \'Could we have the menu?\' Di sini \'menu\' dibaca me-nyu.',
    'Neutral. Add \'please\'. Alternative: \'Could we have the menu?\'',
  ),
  'Are you ready to order?': VocabUsage(
    'Are you ready to order? - Could we have a few more minutes?',
    '',
    'Sudah siap memesan? - Boleh minta waktu beberapa menit lagi?',
    '',
    'Netral. Pertanyaan pelayan. Jika belum siap: \'Not yet, could we have a minute?\'',
    'Neutral. A server\'s question. If not ready: \'Not yet, could we have a minute?\'',
  ),
  'What do you recommend?': VocabUsage(
    'It\'s my first time here. What do you recommend?',
    '',
    'Ini pertama kali saya ke sini. Apa yang Anda rekomendasikan?',
    '',
    'Netral. Jangan tambah \'me\' langsung: bukan \'recommend me\'. Pakai \'What would you recommend?\' agar lebih sopan.',
    'Neutral. Don\'t say \'recommend me\'. \'What would you recommend?\' is politer.',
  ),
  'I\'ll have the same': VocabUsage(
    'The steak sounds good. I\'ll have the same, please.',
    '',
    'Steiknya kedengarannya enak. Saya pesan yang sama.',
    '',
    'Netral. Untuk memesan seperti orang sebelumnya. Untuk pesan lain: \'I\'ll have the..., please.\'',
    'Neutral. To order what the previous person ordered. Otherwise: \'I\'ll have the..., please.\'',
  ),
  'For here or to go?': VocabUsage(
    'One iced latte. - For here or to go? - To go, please.',
    '',
    'Satu es latte. - Makan di sini atau dibawa pulang? - Dibawa pulang.',
    '',
    'Netral, khas Amerika. Versi Inggris: \'Eat in or take away?\'',
    'Neutral, American. British version: \'Eat in or take away?\'',
  ),
  'Anything else?': VocabUsage(
    'Two burgers and a coke. Anything else? - No, that\'s it.',
    '',
    'Dua burger dan satu cola. Ada lagi? - Tidak, itu saja.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pertanyaan kasir/pelayan. Jawab \'That\'s all\' atau \'No, that\'s it, thanks.\'',
    'Neutral. A cashier or server\'s question. Reply \'That\'s all\' or \'No, that\'s it, thanks.\'',
  ),
  'That\'s all': VocabUsage(
    'Just a coffee and a muffin. That\'s all, thanks.',
    '',
    'Kopi dan muffin saja. Itu saja, makasih.',
    '',
    'Netral. Menandakan pesanan selesai. Variasi: \'That\'s it.\' Tambahkan \'thanks\' agar ramah.',
    'Neutral. Signals your order is complete. Variation: \'That\'s it.\' Add \'thanks\' to sound friendly.',
  ),
  'Can I get the bill?': VocabUsage(
    'Excuse me, can I get the bill, please?',
    '',
    'Permisi, boleh minta bonnya?',
    '',
    'Netral. Inggris \'the bill\', Amerika \'the check\'. Jangan minta \'the bill\' sambil berteriak; angkat tangan saja.',
    'Neutral. UK \'the bill\', US \'the check\'. Catch the server\'s eye rather than calling out.',
  ),
  'Can we split the bill?': VocabUsage(
    'Can we split the bill? We\'ll each pay for our own food.',
    '',
    'Bisa bayar sendiri-sendiri? Kami masing-masing bayar makanan sendiri.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa juga \'split it evenly\' (dibagi rata). Di Amerika: \'separate checks\'.',
    'Neutral. Also \'split it evenly\'. In the US: \'separate checks\'.',
  ),
  'It\'s on me': VocabUsage(
    'Put your wallet away. It\'s on me tonight.',
    '',
    'Simpan dompetmu. Malam ini biar saya yang traktir.',
    '',
    'Santai. Pola: \'(Something) is on me\'. Balasan: \'Are you sure? Next one\'s on me, then.\'',
    'Casual. Pattern: \'(Something) is on me\'. Reply: \'Are you sure? Next one\'s on me, then.\'',
  ),
  'Who\'s calling, please?': VocabUsage(
    'Can I speak to Mr. Lee? - Who\'s calling, please?',
    '',
    'Bisa bicara dengan Pak Lee? - Dengan siapa saya bicara?',
    '',
    'Sopan/formal. Dipakai resepsionis atau saat menerima telepon untuk orang lain. Hindari \'Who are you?\' yang terdengar kasar.',
    'Polite/formal. Used when answering for someone else. Avoid \'Who are you?\', which sounds rude.',
  ),
  'Speaking': VocabUsage(
    'Hello, may I speak to Dina? - Speaking.',
    '',
    'Halo, bisa bicara dengan Dina? - Ya, saya sendiri.',
    '',
    'Netral. Jawaban di telepon saat orang yang dicari adalah Anda sendiri. Versi lain: \'This is she/he.\'',
    'Neutral. Phone reply when you are the person asked for. Also: \'This is she/he.\'',
  ),
  'Can I take a message?': VocabUsage(
    'She\'s in a meeting right now. Can I take a message?',
    '',
    'Dia sedang rapat. Mau titip pesan?',
    '',
    'Netral. Ditawarkan saat orang yang dicari tidak ada. Pihak penelepon bilang \'Can I leave a message?\' (leave, bukan take).',
    'Neutral. Offered when the person is unavailable. The caller says \'Can I leave a message?\'',
  ),
  'Hold the line, please': VocabUsage(
    'Hold the line, please. I\'ll put you through.',
    '',
    'Mohon tunggu, jangan ditutup dulu. Saya sambungkan.',
    '',
    'Sopan/formal. Khas resepsionis dan layanan pelanggan. Versi santai: \'Hang on a minute.\'',
    'Polite/formal. Typical of receptionists and customer service. Casual: \'Hang on a minute.\'',
  ),
  'You\'ve got the wrong number': VocabUsage(
    'Sorry, there\'s no Budi here. You\'ve got the wrong number.',
    '',
    'Maaf, tidak ada Budi di sini. Anda salah sambung.',
    '',
    'Netral. Awali dengan \'Sorry\' agar tidak ketus. Penelepon menjawab \'Oh, sorry about that.\'',
    'Neutral. Start with \'Sorry\' so it isn\'t curt. The caller replies \'Oh, sorry about that.\'',
  ),
  'I\'ll call you back': VocabUsage(
    'I\'m driving right now. I\'ll call you back in ten minutes.',
    '',
    'Saya sedang menyetir. Nanti saya telepon balik sepuluh menit lagi.',
    '',
    'Netral. Janji menelepon kembali. Jangan bilang \'I\'ll call you again\' kalau maksudnya membalas telepon.',
    'Neutral. Promise to return a call. \'Call you again\' means another call, not a reply.',
  ),
  'You\'re breaking up': VocabUsage(
    'Sorry, you\'re breaking up. Can you move somewhere with a better signal?',
    '',
    'Maaf, suaramu putus-putus. Bisa pindah ke tempat yang sinyalnya lebih bagus?',
    '',
    'Netral. Soal sinyal, bukan putus hubungan cinta. Jangan salah paham dengan \'break up with\'.',
    'Neutral. About bad signal, not a relationship break-up.',
  ),
  'Can you hear me?': VocabUsage(
    'Can you hear me? I think my mic was muted.',
    '',
    'Suaraku terdengar? Sepertinya mikrofonku tadi mati.',
    '',
    'Netral. Wajib di rapat daring. Jawaban: \'Loud and clear.\' Jangan \'Can you listen me?\'.',
    'Neutral. Essential in online meetings. Reply: \'Loud and clear.\'',
  ),
  'Is now a good time?': VocabUsage(
    'Hi, it\'s Andi. Is now a good time? It\'ll only take a minute.',
    '',
    'Halo, ini Andi. Sekarang waktunya pas? Cuma sebentar kok.',
    '',
    'Sopan/formal. Ditanyakan di awal telepon agar tidak mengganggu. Variasi: \'Is this a bad time?\'',
    'Polite/formal. Asked at the start of a call to avoid interrupting. Variation: \'Is this a bad time?\'',
  ),
  'Sorry I missed your call': VocabUsage(
    'Hi, sorry I missed your call. I was in the shower.',
    '',
    'Hai, maaf tadi tidak sempat angkat teleponmu. Saya lagi mandi.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pembuka saat menelepon balik. \'Miss\' di sini artinya terlewat, bukan rindu.',
    'Neutral. Opener when returning a call. \'Miss\' here means fail to answer.',
  ),
  'Are you free on Friday?': VocabUsage(
    'Are you free on Friday? Let\'s grab lunch.',
    '',
    'Kamu kosong hari Jumat? Yuk makan siang bareng.',
    '',
    'Santai. \'Free\' artinya tidak sibuk, bukan gratis. Pakai \'on\' untuk hari: on Friday.',
    'Casual. \'Free\' means not busy, not costless. Use \'on\' with days.',
  ),
  'What time works for you?': VocabUsage(
    'We need to meet this week. What time works for you?',
    '',
    'Kita perlu ketemu minggu ini. Jam berapa yang cocok untukmu?',
    '',
    'Netral. \'Work\' di sini artinya cocok. Jawaban: \'Anytime after 3 works for me.\'',
    'Neutral. \'Work\' means suit. Reply: \'Anytime after 3 works for me.\'',
  ),
  'How about Monday?': VocabUsage(
    'I\'m busy on Friday. How about Monday?',
    '',
    'Saya sibuk hari Jumat. Bagaimana kalau Senin?',
    '',
    'Netral. Menawarkan alternatif waktu. Setelah \'How about\' pakai kata benda atau V-ing.',
    'Neutral. Suggests an alternative. After \'How about\' use a noun or V-ing.',
  ),
  'Let me check my calendar': VocabUsage(
    'Next Tuesday? Let me check my calendar.',
    '',
    'Selasa depan? Coba saya cek jadwal dulu.',
    '',
    'Netral. Menunda menjawab ajakan sampai yakin jadwal kosong. \'Calendar\' dibaca ke-len-der.',
    'Neutral. Delays answering until you\'ve checked you\'re free.',
  ),
  'I\'d like to make an appointment': VocabUsage(
    'Hello, I\'d like to make an appointment with Dr. Hasan.',
    '',
    'Halo, saya ingin membuat janji temu dengan Dr. Hasan.',
    '',
    'Sopan/formal. Untuk dokter, bank, atau kantor layanan. Pakai \'make\', bukan \'do an appointment\'. Untuk teman pakai \'make plans\'.',
    'Polite/formal. For doctors, banks or offices. Use \'make\', not \'do\'. With friends, say \'make plans\'.',
  ),
  'I need to reschedule': VocabUsage(
    'I\'m sorry, I need to reschedule our meeting to Thursday.',
    '',
    'Maaf, saya perlu mengganti jadwal rapat kita ke Kamis.',
    '',
    'Netral. Ucapkan sedini mungkin dan tawarkan waktu baru. Amerika: ri-ske-jul; Inggris: ri-she-jul.',
    'Neutral. Say it early and suggest a new time. US: ree-SKED-jool; UK: ree-SHED-yool.',
  ),
  'Something came up': VocabUsage(
    'I can\'t make it tonight, sorry. Something came up at work.',
    '',
    'Maaf, saya tidak bisa datang malam ini. Ada urusan mendadak di kantor.',
    '',
    'Santai. Alasan umum membatalkan janji tanpa merinci. Terlalu sering dipakai bisa terdengar seperti alasan saja.',
    'Casual. A common excuse without details. Used too often, it can sound like an excuse.',
  ),
  'I\'m running late': VocabUsage(
    'I\'m running late. I\'ll be there in fifteen minutes.',
    '',
    'Saya bakal agak terlambat. Lima belas menit lagi sampai.',
    '',
    'Netral. Kabari sebelum waktu janji dan sebutkan perkiraan tiba. Lebih wajar daripada \'I will late\'.',
    'Neutral. Let people know beforehand and give an ETA.',
  ),
  'I\'m on my way': VocabUsage(
    'Don\'t start without me! I\'m on my way.',
    '',
    'Jangan mulai tanpa saya! Saya sedang di jalan.',
    '',
    'Santai. Artinya sudah berangkat. Hati-hati: kadang dipakai padahal belum berangkat, jadi jangan disalahgunakan.',
    'Casual. Means you\'ve already left. Don\'t say it if you haven\'t left yet.',
  ),
  'See you then': VocabUsage(
    'Okay, Saturday at seven. See you then!',
    '',
    'Oke, Sabtu jam tujuh. Sampai ketemu nanti!',
    '',
    'Santai. Menutup obrolan sambil mengonfirmasi waktu janjian. \'Then\' merujuk waktu yang baru disepakati.',
    'Casual. Ends the chat while confirming the arranged time. \'Then\' refers to that time.',
  ),
  'What time is it?': VocabUsage(
    'Excuse me, what time is it? My phone died.',
    '',
    'Permisi, jam berapa sekarang? HP saya mati.',
    '',
    'Netral. Ke orang asing awali dengan \'Excuse me\'. Versi sopan: \'Do you have the time?\' (bukan \'Do you have time?\').',
    'Neutral. With strangers, start with \'Excuse me\'. Polite: \'Do you have the time?\' (not \'Do you have time?\').',
  ),
  'get up': VocabUsage(
    'I usually get up at six on weekdays.',
    '',
    'Aku biasanya bangun jam enam pada hari kerja.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tidak memakai objek. Beda dengan wake up (terbangun): get up = bangkit dari kasur. Lampau: got up.',
    'Neutral. Takes no object. Differs from wake up: get up = leave the bed. Past: got up.',
  ),
  'get back': VocabUsage(
    'What time did you get back last night?',
    '',
    'Jam berapa kamu pulang semalam?',
    '',
    'Netral. Pola: get back from/to + tempat. Get sth back = mendapatkan kembali barang. Lampau: got back.',
    'Neutral. Pattern: get back from/to + place. Get sth back = recover an item. Past: got back.',
  ),
  'get out': VocabUsage(
    'Get out of the car slowly and close the door.',
    '',
    'Keluar dari mobil pelan-pelan dan tutup pintunya.',
    '',
    'Netral. Dengan tempat pakai \'of\': get out of the room. \'Get out!\' sendirian terdengar kasar (= keluar sana!).',
    'Neutral. With a place use \'of\': get out of the room. \'Get out!\' alone sounds rude.',
  ),
  'get on': VocabUsage(
    'We got on the train just before the doors closed.',
    '',
    'Kami naik kereta tepat sebelum pintunya menutup.',
    '',
    'Netral. Untuk bus, kereta, pesawat, motor (kendaraan besar/tanpa atap). Untuk mobil/taksi pakai get in. Tidak bisa dipisah.',
    'Neutral. For buses, trains, planes, bikes. For cars/taxis use get in. Not separable.',
  ),
  'get off': VocabUsage(
    'Get off at the next stop and walk to the museum.',
    '',
    'Turun di halte berikutnya lalu jalan kaki ke museum.',
    '',
    'Netral. Lawan get on. Juga: get off work (pulang kerja). Lampau: got off.',
    'Neutral. Opposite of get on. Also: get off work (finish work). Past: got off.',
  ),
  'get in': VocabUsage(
    'Get in, I\'ll drive you home.',
    '',
    'Masuk, aku antar kamu pulang.',
    '',
    'Netral. Untuk mobil/taksi (lawannya get out). Juga berarti tiba: The train gets in at 5. Lampau: got in.',
    'Neutral. For cars/taxis (opposite: get out). Also means arrive: The train gets in at 5. Past: got in.',
  ),
  'get along': VocabUsage(
    'My sister and I get along really well now.',
    '',
    'Aku dan kakakku sekarang akur sekali.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pola: get along with + orang. Versi Inggris British: get on with. Tidak memakai objek langsung.',
    'Neutral. Pattern: get along with + person. British: get on with. Takes no direct object.',
  ),
  'get over': VocabUsage(
    'It took him months to get over the breakup.',
    '',
    'Butuh berbulan-bulan baginya untuk melupakan putusnya hubungan itu.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tidak bisa dipisah: get over it (bukan *get it over). Dipakai untuk sakit, kecewa, patah hati.',
    'Neutral. Not separable: get over it (not *get it over). Used for illness, disappointment, heartbreak.',
  ),
  'get through': VocabUsage(
    'We\'ll get through this together.',
    '',
    'Kita akan melewati ini bersama.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tidak dipisah: get through the exam/winter. Juga: get through (to sb) = tersambung lewat telepon.',
    'Neutral. Not separable: get through the exam/winter. Also: get through (to sb) = connect by phone.',
  ),
  'get away': VocabUsage(
    'We\'re hoping to get away for a few days in August.',
    '',
    'Kami berharap bisa pergi berlibur beberapa hari di bulan Agustus.',
    '',
    'Netral. Get away from = menjauh/kabur dari. Get away with sth = lolos dari hukuman. Lampau: got away.',
    'Neutral. Get away from = escape from. Get away with sth = avoid punishment. Past: got away.',
  ),
  'get together': VocabUsage(
    'Let\'s get together for coffee next week.',
    '',
    'Ayo ketemuan ngopi minggu depan.',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Pola: get together with + orang. Kata benda: a get-together (acara kumpul-kumpul).',
    'Casual/neutral. Pattern: get together with + person. Noun: a get-together.',
  ),
  'get rid of': VocabUsage(
    'I need to get rid of these old clothes.',
    '',
    'Aku perlu menyingkirkan baju-baju lama ini.',
    '',
    'Netral. Selalu + kata benda: get rid of + sth/sb. Juga untuk penyakit: get rid of a cold.',
    'Neutral. Always + noun: get rid of + sth/sb. Also for illness: get rid of a cold.',
  ),
  'get by': VocabUsage(
    'She gets by on a small salary.',
    '',
    'Ia bertahan hidup dengan gaji yang kecil.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pola: get by on/with + sesuatu. Juga: I can get by in English (cukup bisa berkomunikasi).',
    'Neutral. Pattern: get by on/with + something. Also: I can get by in English (manage basically).',
  ),
  'get into': VocabUsage(
    'He got into photography during the pandemic.',
    '',
    'Ia mulai menyukai fotografi selama pandemi.',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Arti lain: masuk (get into a car), diterima (get into university), terlibat (get into trouble).',
    'Casual/neutral. Other meanings: enter (get into a car), be accepted (get into university), get into trouble.',
  ),
  'go on': VocabUsage(
    'What\'s going on here?',
    '',
    'Ada apa di sini?',
    '',
    'Netral. Go on + -ing = terus melakukan: go on talking. \'Go on!\' = silakan, lanjutkan. Lampau: went on.',
    'Neutral. Go on + -ing = continue: go on talking. \'Go on!\' = continue, please. Past: went on.',
  ),
  'go back': VocabUsage(
    'I want to go back to Bali next year.',
    '',
    'Aku ingin kembali ke Bali tahun depan.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pola: go back to + tempat; go back home (tanpa \'to\'). Lampau: went back.',
    'Neutral. Pattern: go back to + place; go back home (no \'to\'). Past: went back.',
  ),
  'go out': VocabUsage(
    'Do you want to go out tonight?',
    '',
    'Kamu mau keluar jalan-jalan malam ini?',
    '',
    'Netral. Juga: lampu/api padam (The lights went out). Go out for dinner/a walk. Lampau: went out.',
    'Neutral. Also: lights/fire stop (The lights went out). Go out for dinner/a walk. Past: went out.',
  ),
  'go down': VocabUsage(
    'The price of petrol went down last month.',
    '',
    'Harga bensin turun bulan lalu.',
    '',
    'Netral. Untuk harga, angka, matahari (the sun went down), atau turun tangga. Lawan go up.',
    'Neutral. For prices, numbers, the sun (the sun went down), or stairs. Opposite: go up.',
  ),
  'go up': VocabUsage(
    'Rents keep going up in this city.',
    '',
    'Harga sewa di kota ini terus naik.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pola: go up by 10% / go up to 50. Juga: naik tangga/lift. Lampau: went up.',
    'Neutral. Pattern: go up by 10% / go up to 50. Also: go upstairs/in a lift. Past: went up.',
  ),
  'go through': VocabUsage(
    'She went through a lot after her father died.',
    '',
    'Ia mengalami banyak hal berat setelah ayahnya meninggal.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tidak dipisah. Arti lain: memeriksa teliti (go through the documents), melewati (go through security).',
    'Neutral. Not separable. Other meanings: examine (go through the documents), pass (go through security).',
  ),
  'go off': VocabUsage(
    'My alarm didn\'t go off this morning.',
    '',
    'Alarmku tidak berbunyi tadi pagi.',
    '',
    'Netral. Untuk alarm, bom (meledak), makanan (basi: the milk has gone off — British). Lampau: went off.',
    'Neutral. For alarms, bombs (explode), food (the milk has gone off — British). Past: went off.',
  ),
  'go away': VocabUsage(
    'Go away — I\'m trying to sleep!',
    '',
    'Pergi sana — aku lagi coba tidur!',
    '',
    'Netral; sebagai perintah terdengar kasar. Juga: rasa sakit hilang (The pain went away), pergi berlibur.',
    'Neutral; as an order it sounds rude. Also: pain disappears (The pain went away), go on holiday.',
  ),
  'go for': VocabUsage(
    'I think I\'ll go for the chicken salad.',
    '',
    'Kayaknya aku pilih salad ayam.',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. \'Go for it!\' = ayo, coba saja! Juga: go for a walk/run (pergi jalan/lari).',
    'Casual/neutral. \'Go for it!\' = try it! Also: go for a walk/run.',
  ),
  'go along with': VocabUsage(
    'I didn\'t like the plan, but I went along with it.',
    '',
    'Aku tidak suka rencana itu, tapi aku ikut saja.',
    '',
    'Netral. Selalu + objek: go along with + ide/orang. Nuansa: setuju walau tidak sepenuhnya yakin.',
    'Neutral. Always + object: go along with + idea/person. Nuance: agree without full conviction.',
  ),
  'go out with': VocabUsage(
    'How long have you been going out with Sam?',
    '',
    'Sudah berapa lama kamu pacaran dengan Sam?',
    '',
    'Santai. Inggris British; Amerika lebih sering \'date\' atau \'go out\' saja. Lampau: went out with.',
    'Casual. Mostly British; American English often uses \'date\'. Past: went out with.',
  ),
  'come back': VocabUsage(
    'Come back soon — we\'ll miss you!',
    '',
    'Cepat kembali ya — kami akan kangen kamu!',
    '',
    'Netral. Come = ke arah pembicara, go = menjauh. Pola: come back to/from + tempat. Lampau: came back.',
    'Neutral. Come = toward the speaker, go = away. Pattern: come back to/from + place. Past: came back.',
  ),
  'come on': VocabUsage(
    'Come on, we\'re going to be late!',
    '',
    'Ayo, kita bakal terlambat!',
    '',
    'Santai. Dipakai untuk menyemangati atau tidak percaya (\'Oh, come on!\'). Juga: lampu/mesin menyala.',
    'Casual. Used to urge or show disbelief (\'Oh, come on!\'). Also: lights/machines start.',
  ),
  'come up': VocabUsage(
    'Something came up at work, so I can\'t join you.',
    '',
    'Ada urusan mendadak di kantor, jadi aku tidak bisa ikut.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tanpa objek. Juga: matahari terbit (the sun came up), topik dibahas. Lampau: came up.',
    'Neutral. No object. Also: the sun came up, a topic is raised. Past: came up.',
  ),
  'come out': VocabUsage(
    'Her new album comes out on Friday.',
    '',
    'Album barunya rilis hari Jumat.',
    '',
    'Netral. Untuk buku/film/lagu terbit, matahari muncul, kebenaran terungkap. Lampau: came out.',
    'Neutral. For books/films/songs released, the sun appearing, the truth emerging. Past: came out.',
  ),
  'come in': VocabUsage(
    'Come in and have a seat.',
    '',
    'Masuk dan silakan duduk.',
    '',
    'Netral. Ucapan sopan untuk tamu. Juga: kereta/pesan masuk, finis (come in first). Lampau: came in.',
    'Neutral. Polite invitation to enter. Also: trains/messages arrive, finish a race (come in first). Past: came in.',
  ),
  'come along': VocabUsage(
    'We\'re going to the beach — want to come along?',
    '',
    'Kami mau ke pantai — mau ikut?',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Juga menanyakan kemajuan: How\'s your project coming along? Lampau: came along.',
    'Casual/neutral. Also asks about progress: How\'s your project coming along? Past: came along.',
  ),
  'come across': VocabUsage(
    'I came across an old photo of my grandparents.',
    '',
    'Aku tak sengaja menemukan foto lama kakek-nenekku.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tidak dipisah: come across it. Come across as = terkesan (He comes across as shy).',
    'Neutral. Not separable: come across it. Come across as = seem (He comes across as shy).',
  ),
  'come over': VocabUsage(
    'Why don\'t you come over for dinner on Saturday?',
    '',
    'Bagaimana kalau kamu datang makan malam ke rumah hari Sabtu?',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Tanpa objek; tujuan pakai \'to\': come over to my place. Lampau: came over.',
    'Casual/neutral. No object; destination with \'to\': come over to my place. Past: came over.',
  ),
  'come down': VocabUsage(
    'House prices have finally come down a little.',
    '',
    'Harga rumah akhirnya turun sedikit.',
    '',
    'Netral. Juga: turun dari atas (Come down from the roof!). Lampau: came down.',
    'Neutral. Also: descend (Come down from the roof!). Past: came down.',
  ),
  'come down with': VocabUsage(
    'I think I\'m coming down with the flu.',
    '',
    'Kayaknya aku mau kena flu.',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Untuk penyakit ringan: come down with a cold/fever. Tidak dipisah.',
    'Casual/neutral. For minor illnesses: come down with a cold/fever. Not separable.',
  ),
  'take off': VocabUsage(
    'Our plane took off an hour late.',
    '',
    'Pesawat kami lepas landas terlambat satu jam.',
    '',
    'Netral. Arti \'melepas\' bisa dipisah: take your shoes off / take off your shoes. Juga: cuti (take a day off). Lampau: took off.',
    'Neutral. \'Remove\' is separable: take your shoes off / take off your shoes. Also: take a day off. Past: took off.',
  ),
  'take on': VocabUsage(
    'She took on too much work this month.',
    '',
    'Ia menerima terlalu banyak pekerjaan bulan ini.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: take it on. Juga: merekrut (take on new staff), melawan (take on a rival).',
    'Neutral. Separable: take it on. Also: hire (take on new staff), compete against (take on a rival).',
  ),
  'take out': VocabUsage(
    'Can you take out the rubbish, please?',
    '',
    'Tolong buang sampahnya ke luar, ya?',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: take it out. Take sb out = mengajak makan/kencan. Juga: tarik uang (take out cash).',
    'Neutral. Separable: take it out. Take sb out = invite on a date/meal. Also: take out cash.',
  ),
  'take up': VocabUsage(
    'My dad took up yoga after he retired.',
    '',
    'Ayahku mulai menekuni yoga setelah pensiun.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: take it up. Juga: menyita (The sofa takes up too much space).',
    'Neutral. Separable: take it up. Also: occupy (The sofa takes up too much space).',
  ),
  'take back': VocabUsage(
    'I took the shoes back because they were too small.',
    '',
    'Aku mengembalikan sepatunya karena terlalu kecil.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: take it back. \'I take it back\' = aku tarik kata-kataku. Lampau: took back.',
    'Neutral. Separable: take it back. \'I take it back\' = I withdraw what I said. Past: took back.',
  ),
  'take in': VocabUsage(
    'There was too much information to take in at once.',
    '',
    'Terlalu banyak informasi untuk dipahami sekaligus.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: take it in. Juga: menampung (take in a stray cat), mengecilkan baju.',
    'Neutral. Separable: take it in. Also: give shelter (take in a stray cat), make clothes smaller.',
  ),
  'take away': VocabUsage(
    'The waiter took away our plates.',
    '',
    'Pelayan mengambil piring-piring kami.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: take them away. British: takeaway = makanan bungkus. Lampau: took away.',
    'Neutral. Separable: take them away. British: takeaway = food to go. Past: took away.',
  ),
  'take down': VocabUsage(
    'They took down the posters after the event.',
    '',
    'Mereka menurunkan poster-poster setelah acara.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: take them down. Juga: mencatat (take down notes), menghapus postingan.',
    'Neutral. Separable: take them down. Also: write (take down notes), remove an online post.',
  ),
  'take after': VocabUsage(
    'She really takes after her mother.',
    '',
    'Dia benar-benar mirip ibunya.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tidak dipisah dan tidak dipakai bentuk -ing/pasif. Untuk keluarga yang lebih tua (ayah, ibu, kakek).',
    'Neutral. Not separable; not used in -ing or passive. For older relatives (parents, grandparents).',
  ),
  'put on': VocabUsage(
    'Put on your jacket — it\'s cold outside.',
    '',
    'Pakai jaketmu — di luar dingin.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: put it on (bukan *put on it). Put on = aksi memakai; wear = keadaan memakai. Juga: put on weight.',
    'Neutral. Separable: put it on (not *put on it). Put on = the action; wear = the state. Also: put on weight.',
  ),
  'put off': VocabUsage(
    'Stop putting off your homework!',
    '',
    'Berhenti menunda-nunda PR-mu!',
    '',
    'Netral. Pola: put off + -ing (put off going). Bisa dipisah: put it off. Juga: membuat ilfil (The smell put me off).',
    'Neutral. Pattern: put off + -ing (put off going). Separable: put it off. Also: discourage (The smell put me off).',
  ),
  'put out': VocabUsage(
    'Firefighters put out the fire in twenty minutes.',
    '',
    'Pemadam kebakaran memadamkan api dalam dua puluh menit.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: put it out. Untuk api, rokok, lilin. Lampau: put out (tidak berubah).',
    'Neutral. Separable: put it out. For fires, cigarettes, candles. Past: put out (unchanged).',
  ),
  'put up': VocabUsage(
    'We put up a tent near the lake.',
    '',
    'Kami memasang tenda di dekat danau.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: put it up. Juga: menaikkan harga, menginapkan tamu (put sb up for the night).',
    'Neutral. Separable: put it up. Also: raise prices, give a guest a bed (put sb up for the night).',
  ),
  'put down': VocabUsage(
    'Put the box down here, please.',
    '',
    'Tolong taruh kotaknya di sini.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: put it down. Juga: merendahkan orang (put sb down), menidurkan bayi.',
    'Neutral. Separable: put it down. Also: insult (put sb down), put a baby to bed.',
  ),
  'put away': VocabUsage(
    'Please put your toys away before dinner.',
    '',
    'Tolong simpan mainanmu sebelum makan malam.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: put them away. Juga: menabung (put money away).',
    'Neutral. Separable: put them away. Also: save (put money away).',
  ),
  'put back': VocabUsage(
    'Put the milk back in the fridge when you\'re done.',
    '',
    'Kembalikan susunya ke kulkas kalau sudah selesai.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: put it back. Juga: menunda jadwal (The meeting was put back to Friday).',
    'Neutral. Separable: put it back. Also: postpone (The meeting was put back to Friday).',
  ),
  'put up with': VocabUsage(
    'I can\'t put up with this noise any longer.',
    '',
    'Aku tidak tahan lagi dengan kebisingan ini.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tidak dipisah: put up with it. Sering negatif: can\'t put up with. Mirip tolerate/stand.',
    'Neutral. Not separable: put up with it. Often negative: can\'t put up with. Similar to tolerate/stand.',
  ),
  'put in': VocabUsage(
    'She put in a lot of effort to pass the exam.',
    '',
    'Ia mencurahkan banyak usaha agar lulus ujian.',
    '',
    'Netral. Juga: memasang (put in a new kitchen), mengajukan (put in a request). Bisa dipisah: put it in.',
    'Neutral. Also: install (put in a new kitchen), submit (put in a request). Separable: put it in.',
  ),
  'look for': VocabUsage(
    'I\'m looking for my keys — have you seen them?',
    '',
    'Aku lagi mencari kunciku — kamu lihat?',
    '',
    'Netral. Tidak dipisah: look for it (bukan *look it for). Look for = proses mencari; find = berhasil menemukan.',
    'Neutral. Not separable: look for it (not *look it for). Look for = the search; find = the result.',
  ),
  'look after': VocabUsage(
    'Can you look after my cat this weekend?',
    '',
    'Bisa tolong jaga kucingku akhir pekan ini?',
    '',
    'Netral. Tidak dipisah: look after him. Lebih British; Amerika sering take care of.',
    'Neutral. Not separable: look after him. More British; American often says take care of.',
  ),
  'look up': VocabUsage(
    'If you don\'t know the word, look it up.',
    '',
    'Kalau kamu tidak tahu katanya, cari saja di kamus.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: look it up (bukan *look up it). Tanpa objek = menengadah; things are looking up = membaik.',
    'Neutral. Separable: look it up (not *look up it). No object = raise your eyes; things are looking up = improving.',
  ),
  'look out': VocabUsage(
    'Look out! There\'s a car coming!',
    '',
    'Awas! Ada mobil datang!',
    '',
    'Netral. Biasanya seruan peringatan. Mirip watch out. Juga: melihat keluar (look out of the window).',
    'Neutral. Usually a warning shout. Similar to watch out. Also: look out of the window.',
  ),
  'look around': VocabUsage(
    'We spent the afternoon looking around the old town.',
    '',
    'Kami menghabiskan sore melihat-lihat kota tua.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dengan atau tanpa objek: look around (the shop). British juga: look round.',
    'Neutral. With or without object: look around (the shop). British also: look round.',
  ),
  'look back': VocabUsage(
    'Looking back, I should have studied harder.',
    '',
    'Kalau dikenang lagi, seharusnya aku belajar lebih giat.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pola: look back on/at + masa lalu. \'Looking back,\' sering di awal kalimat.',
    'Neutral. Pattern: look back on/at + the past. \'Looking back,\' often starts a sentence.',
  ),
  'look through': VocabUsage(
    'I looked through my notes before the test.',
    '',
    'Aku membaca sekilas catatanku sebelum ujian.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tidak dipisah: look through it. Juga: mencari-cari di dalam (look through my bag).',
    'Neutral. Not separable: look through it. Also: search inside (look through my bag).',
  ),
  'look up to': VocabUsage(
    'Many kids look up to their older brothers.',
    '',
    'Banyak anak mengagumi kakak laki-laki mereka.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tidak dipisah: look up to him. Lawan: look down on.',
