    '',
    'Ia keluar dari kuliah untuk memulai bisnis.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pola: drop out of + sekolah/lomba. Kata benda: a dropout (orang yang putus sekolah).',
    'Neutral. Pattern: drop out of + school/race. Noun: a dropout.',
  ),
  'pull out': VocabUsage(
    'The dentist pulled out my bad tooth.',
    '',
    'Dokter gigi mencabut gigiku yang rusak.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: pull it out. Tanpa objek = mundur (pull out of the deal) atau mobil keluar ke jalan.',
    'Neutral. Separable: pull it out. No object = withdraw (pull out of the deal) or a car moving into traffic.',
  ),
  'pull over': VocabUsage(
    'The police told the driver to pull over.',
    '',
    'Polisi menyuruh pengemudi menepi.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tanpa objek = menepi sendiri. Pull sb over = polisi menghentikan pengemudi.',
    'Neutral. No object = stop at the side. Pull sb over = police stop a driver.',
  ),
  'wake up': VocabUsage(
    'I woke up in the middle of the night.',
    '',
    'Aku terbangun tengah malam.',
    '',
    'Netral. Lampau: woke up. Bisa dipisah dengan objek: wake me up at seven.',
    'Neutral. Past: woke up. Separable with an object: wake me up at seven.',
  ),
  'grow up': VocabUsage(
    'I grew up in a small village near Solo.',
    '',
    'Aku tumbuh besar di desa kecil dekat Solo.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tanpa objek. \'Grow up!\' = jangan kekanak-kanakan. Lampau: grew up. Kata benda: grown-up.',
    'Neutral. No object. \'Grow up!\' = stop being childish. Past: grew up. Noun: a grown-up.',
  ),
  'end up': VocabUsage(
    'We got lost and ended up in a different town.',
    '',
    'Kami tersesat dan akhirnya sampai di kota lain.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pola: end up + -ing (ended up staying), end up in/at + tempat.',
    'Neutral. Pattern: end up + -ing (ended up staying), end up in/at + place.',
  ),
  'clean up': VocabUsage(
    'Let\'s clean up the kitchen before Mum gets home.',
    '',
    'Ayo bereskan dapur sebelum Ibu pulang.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: clean it up. Clean up after sb = membereskan kekacauan orang lain.',
    'Neutral. Separable: clean it up. Clean up after sb = tidy their mess.',
  ),
  'hurry up': VocabUsage(
    'Hurry up, the bus is leaving!',
    '',
    'Cepat, busnya mau berangkat!',
    '',
    'Santai. Biasanya perintah. Hurry sb up = menyuruh bergegas.',
    'Casual. Usually an order. Hurry sb up = make sb go faster.',
  ),
  'back up': VocabUsage(
    'Always back up your files before updating.',
    '',
    'Selalu cadangkan file-mu sebelum memperbarui.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: back it up. Juga: mendukung (back me up), mundur (mobil). Kata benda: a backup.',
    'Neutral. Separable: back it up. Also: support (back me up), reverse a car. Noun: a backup.',
  ),
  'warm up': VocabUsage(
    'Always warm up before you go running.',
    '',
    'Selalu lakukan pemanasan sebelum lari.',
    '',
    'Netral. Dengan objek = menghangatkan (warm up the soup), bisa dipisah: warm it up. Kata benda: a warm-up.',
    'Neutral. With object = heat (warm up the soup), separable: warm it up. Noun: a warm-up.',
  ),
  'cheer up': VocabUsage(
    'Cheer up — it\'s not the end of the world!',
    '',
    'Ayo semangat — ini bukan akhir dunia!',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Tanpa objek = jadi ceria; cheer sb up = menghibur (bisa dipisah: cheer her up).',
    'Casual/neutral. No object = become happier; cheer sb up = make sb happier (separable: cheer her up).',
  ),
  'mix up': VocabUsage(
    'I always mix up the twins\' names.',
    '',
    'Aku selalu tertukar nama si kembar.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: mix them up. Pola: mix up A with B. Kata benda: a mix-up (salah paham).',
    'Neutral. Separable: mix them up. Pattern: mix up A with B. Noun: a mix-up.',
  ),
  'fill up': VocabUsage(
    'Let\'s fill up the tank before the trip.',
    '',
    'Ayo isi penuh tangki sebelum perjalanan.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: fill it up. Tanpa objek = menjadi penuh (The room filled up quickly).',
    'Neutral. Separable: fill it up. No object = become full (The room filled up quickly).',
  ),
  'sit down': VocabUsage(
    'Please sit down and make yourself comfortable.',
    '',
    'Silakan duduk dan buat dirimu nyaman.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tanpa objek. Lampau: sat down. Lawan: stand up.',
    'Neutral. No object. Past: sat down. Opposite: stand up.',
  ),
  'calm down': VocabUsage(
    'Calm down and tell me what happened.',
    '',
    'Tenang dulu dan ceritakan apa yang terjadi.',
    '',
    'Netral. \'Calm down!\' ke orang yang marah bisa terdengar menyulut. Calm sb down = menenangkan.',
    'Neutral. Saying \'Calm down!\' to an angry person can sound provocative. Calm sb down = soothe sb.',
  ),
  'slow down': VocabUsage(
    'Slow down — there\'s a school ahead.',
    '',
    'Pelan-pelan — ada sekolah di depan.',
    '',
    'Netral. Dengan atau tanpa objek: slow the car down. Juga: hidup lebih santai.',
    'Neutral. With or without object: slow the car down. Also: take life more easily.',
  ),
  'settle down': VocabUsage(
    'They got married and settled down in Yogyakarta.',
    '',
    'Mereka menikah dan menetap di Yogyakarta.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tanpa objek. Juga: menjadi tenang (The class settled down).',
    'Neutral. No object. Also: become calm (The class settled down).',
  ),
  'write down': VocabUsage(
    'Write down your password somewhere safe.',
    '',
    'Catat kata sandimu di tempat yang aman.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: write it down (bukan *write down it). Lampau: wrote down.',
    'Neutral. Separable: write it down (not *write down it). Past: wrote down.',
  ),
  'lie down': VocabUsage(
    'I need to lie down for a few minutes.',
    '',
    'Aku perlu berbaring beberapa menit.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tanpa objek. Lampau: lay down (jangan tertukar dengan lay = meletakkan). Bentuk -ing: lying.',
    'Neutral. No object. Past: lay down (don\'t confuse with lay = put). -ing form: lying.',
  ),
  'let down': VocabUsage(
    'I promised to help, and I won\'t let you down.',
    '',
    'Aku sudah janji membantu, dan aku tidak akan mengecewakanmu.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: let me down. Lampau: let down (tidak berubah). Kata benda: a letdown.',
    'Neutral. Separable: let me down. Past: let down (unchanged). Noun: a letdown.',
  ),
  'find out': VocabUsage(
    'I found out the truth from her sister.',
    '',
    'Aku mengetahui kebenarannya dari kakaknya.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pola: find out + that/wh-: find out where he lives. Bisa dipisah: find it out (jarang). Lampau: found out.',
    'Neutral. Pattern: find out + that/wh-: find out where he lives. Separable but rare: find it out. Past: found out.',
  ),
  'work out': VocabUsage(
    'I work out at the gym three times a week.',
    '',
    'Aku berolahraga di gym tiga kali seminggu.',
    '',
    'Netral. Juga: berhasil (It all worked out), menghitung/memecahkan (work out the answer — bisa dipisah: work it out).',
    'Neutral. Also: succeed (It all worked out), calculate/solve (work out the answer — separable: work it out).',
  ),
  'check out': VocabUsage(
    'We have to check out before noon.',
    '',
    'Kita harus check-out sebelum tengah hari.',
    '',
    'Santai/netral. Juga: lihat/coba (Check out this video!), bayar di kasir. Bisa dipisah: check it out.',
    'Casual/neutral. Also: look at (Check out this video!), pay at a till. Separable: check it out.',
  ),
  'check in': VocabUsage(
    'Please check in at least two hours before your flight.',
    '',
    'Silakan check-in paling lambat dua jam sebelum penerbangan.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pola: check in at + hotel/bandara; check in on sb = menanyakan kabar. Kata benda: check-in.',
    'Neutral. Pattern: check in at + hotel/airport; check in on sb = see how sb is. Noun: check-in.',
  ),
  'work on': VocabUsage(
    'I\'m working on my pronunciation this month.',
    '',
    'Bulan ini aku sedang memperbaiki pengucapanku.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tidak dipisah: work on + proyek/keterampilan. Sering bentuk -ing: I\'m working on it.',
    'Neutral. Not separable: work on + project/skill. Often in -ing: I\'m working on it.',
  ),
  'sort out': VocabUsage(
    'Don\'t worry, we\'ll sort out the problem tomorrow.',
    '',
    'Tenang, besok kita bereskan masalahnya.',
    '',
    'Netral, lebih British. Bisa dipisah: sort it out. Juga: merapikan barang (sort out the cupboard).',
    'Neutral, more British. Separable: sort it out. Also: tidy things (sort out the cupboard).',
  ),
  'move on': VocabUsage(
    'It\'s time to forget the past and move on.',
    '',
    'Saatnya melupakan masa lalu dan melanjutkan hidup.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pola: move on to + topik/tahap berikutnya (Let\'s move on to question 2).',
    'Neutral. Pattern: move on to + next topic/stage (Let\'s move on to question 2).',
  ),
  'hand out': VocabUsage(
    'The teacher handed out the exam papers.',
    '',
    'Guru membagikan lembar ujian.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: hand them out. Kata benda: a handout (lembar materi; bantuan uang).',
    'Neutral. Separable: hand them out. Noun: a handout (printed notes; free money/food).',
  ),
  'throw away': VocabUsage(
    'Don\'t throw away plastic bottles — recycle them.',
    '',
    'Jangan buang botol plastik — daur ulang saja.',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: throw it away (bukan *throw away it). Juga: menyia-nyiakan peluang. Lampau: threw away.',
    'Neutral. Separable: throw it away (not *throw away it). Also: waste a chance. Past: threw away.',
  ),
  'try on': VocabUsage(
    'Can I try on these jeans?',
    '',
    'Boleh aku coba celana jins ini?',
    '',
    'Netral. Bisa dipisah: try them on. Hanya untuk pakaian, sepatu, aksesori.',
    'Neutral. Separable: try them on. Only for clothes, shoes and accessories.',
  ),
  'count on': VocabUsage(
    'You can count on me — I\'ll be there.',
    '',
    'Kamu bisa mengandalkanku — aku pasti datang.',
    '',
    'Netral. Tidak dipisah: count on + orang/hal. Mirip rely on / depend on.',
    'Neutral. Not separable: count on + person/thing. Similar to rely on / depend on.',
  ),
  'fit in': VocabUsage(
    'It took me a while to fit in at my new school.',
