    'Tiketnya habis dalam sejam — kalau nggak beli cepat, ya ketinggalan.',
    '',
    'Santai. Biasanya lampau: I missed the boat. Bukan soal kapal sungguhan.',
    'Casual. Usually past: I missed the boat. Not about a real boat.',
  ),
  'strike while the iron is hot': VocabUsage(
    'Prices are low right now, so strike while the iron is hot.',
    '',
    'Harga sedang turun, jadi manfaatkan kesempatan selagi ada.',
    '',
    'Netral. Peribahasa berbentuk saran. Mirip \'mumpung masih ada kesempatan\'.',
    'Neutral. A proverb used as advice: act while the chance is there.',
  ),
  'a long shot': VocabUsage(
    'It\'s a long shot, but maybe the shop still has one left.',
    '',
    'Peluangnya tipis, tapi mungkin tokonya masih punya satu.',
    '',
    'Santai. Pola: It\'s a long shot, but... Juga: not by a long shot = sama sekali tidak.',
    'Casual. Pattern: It\'s a long shot, but... Also: not by a long shot = not at all.',
  ),
  'once in a lifetime': VocabUsage(
    'Seeing the northern lights was a once-in-a-lifetime experience.',
    '',
    'Melihat aurora itu pengalaman sekali seumur hidup.',
    '',
    'Netral. Sebelum kata benda pakai tanda hubung: a once-in-a-lifetime chance.',
    'Neutral. Hyphenate before a noun: a once-in-a-lifetime chance.',
  ),
  'cost an arm and a leg': VocabUsage(
    'That new phone costs an arm and a leg.',
    '',
    'HP baru itu mahalnya minta ampun.',
    '',
    'Santai. Subjeknya barang: It costs an arm and a leg. Bukan soal kehilangan anggota tubuh.',
    'Casual. Subject is the item: It costs an arm and a leg. Not about losing body parts.',
  ),
  'break the bank': VocabUsage(
    'A weekend trip to Bandung won\'t break the bank.',
    '',
    'Liburan akhir pekan ke Bandung nggak bakal bikin bangkrut.',
    '',
    'Santai. Paling sering negatif: It won\'t break the bank = tidak mahal.',
    'Casual. Most often negative: It won\'t break the bank = it\'s affordable.',
  ),
  'pay through the nose': VocabUsage(
    'We ended up paying through the nose for last-minute tickets.',
    '',
    'Akhirnya kami bayar mahal banget untuk tiket mendadak.',
    '',
    'Santai. Pola: pay through the nose for + benda. Bukan soal hidung.',
    'Casual. Pattern: pay through the nose for + noun. Not about noses.',
  ),
  'make ends meet': VocabUsage(
    'With rent going up, many families struggle to make ends meet.',
    '',
    'Dengan sewa yang naik, banyak keluarga kesulitan mencukupi kebutuhan hidup.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pola: struggle to / barely make ends meet. Mirip \'gali lubang tutup lubang\' tapi tanpa unsur utang.',
    'Neutral. Pattern: struggle to / barely make ends meet.',
  ),
  'tighten your belt': VocabUsage(
    'After I lost my job, we had to tighten our belts.',
    '',
    'Setelah aku kehilangan pekerjaan, kami harus berhemat ketat.',
    '',
    'Netral. Possesif menyesuaikan: tighten our/their belts. Padanannya \'mengencangkan ikat pinggang\'.',
    'Neutral. Possessive changes: tighten our/their belts.',
  ),
  'on a shoestring': VocabUsage(
    'They started the café on a shoestring and grew it slowly.',
    '',
    'Mereka memulai kafe itu dengan modal pas-pasan lalu mengembangkannya pelan-pelan.',
    '',
    'Netral. Pola: on a shoestring (budget). Bukan soal tali sepatu.',
    'Neutral. Pattern: on a shoestring (budget). Not about shoelaces.',
  ),
  'strapped for cash': VocabUsage(
    'Can you pay this time? I\'m a bit strapped for cash.',
    '',
    'Kamu bisa bayar kali ini? Aku lagi agak bokek.',
    '',
    'Santai. Pola: be strapped for cash. Biasanya kondisi sementara.',
    'Casual. Pattern: be strapped for cash. Usually a temporary state.',
  ),
  'live from paycheck to paycheck': VocabUsage(
    'Many young workers live from paycheck to paycheck.',
    '',
