    'Saya jalan-jalan sebentar untuk menjernihkan pikiran.',
    'I\'ll take a short walk to clear my head.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'mendinginkan kepala\', artinya rehat sejenak dari stres atau belajar.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'cool one\'s head\': take a short break from stress or study.',
  ),
  '낯을 가리다': VocabUsage(
    '우리 아이는 낯을 가리는 편이에요.',
    'uri aineun nacheul garineun pyeonieyo.',
    'Anak kami agak malu dengan orang yang belum dikenal.',
    'Our child tends to be shy around strangers.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Artinya canggung atau malu dengan orang baru. Sering untuk anak kecil, juga orang dewasa yang pemalu.',
    'Polite (해요체). Awkward or shy with new people; often said of small children, also shy adults.',
  ),
  '식은 죽 먹기': VocabUsage(
    '이 정도 문제는 식은 죽 먹기예요.',
    'i jeongdo munjeneun sigeun juk meokgiyeyo.',
    'Soal begini sih gampang banget.',
    'A problem like this is a piece of cake.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'makan bubur yang sudah dingin\', artinya sangat mudah. Sinonim: 누워서 떡 먹기.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'eating cold porridge\': very easy. Synonym: 누워서 떡 먹기.',
  ),
  '그림의 떡': VocabUsage(
    '돈이 없으니 저 차는 그림의 떡이에요.',
    'doni eopseuni jeo chaneun geurimui tteogieyo.',
    'Nggak punya uang, mobil itu cuma angan-angan.',
    'With no money, that car is just pie in the sky.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'kue beras dalam lukisan\': diinginkan tapi tak bisa didapat. Mirip \'bagai pungguk merindukan bulan\'.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'rice cake in a painting\': something you want but can\'t have.',
  ),
  '미역국을 먹다': VocabUsage(
    '운전면허 시험에서 또 미역국을 먹었어요.',
    'unjeonmyeonheo siheomeseo tto miyeokgugeul meogeosseoyo.',
    'Saya gagal lagi di ujian SIM.',
    'I failed my driving test again.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'makan sup rumput laut\' (licin, \'tergelincir\'), artinya gagal ujian. Karena itu dihindari sebelum ujian, padahal wajib saat ulang tahun.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'eat seaweed soup\' (slippery), meaning fail an exam. Avoided before exams, yet eaten on birthdays.',
  ),
  '바람을 맞다': VocabUsage(
    '어제 소개팅에서 바람을 맞았어요.',
    'eoje sogaetingeseo barameul majasseoyo.',
    'Kemarin saya ditinggal nggak datang di kencan buta.',
    'I got stood up on a blind date yesterday.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Artinya janji tidak ditepati dan ditunggu sia-sia. Pelakunya: 바람을 맞히다. Jangan tertukar dengan 바람을 피우다 (selingkuh).',
    'Polite (해요체). To be stood up. The one who does it: 바람을 맞히다. Don\'t confuse with 바람을 피우다 (to cheat).',
  ),
  '국수를 먹다': VocabUsage(
    '두 사람 언제 국수를 먹여 줄 거예요?',
    'du saram eonje guksureul meogyeo jul geoyeyo?',
    'Kalian berdua kapan nikahnya?',
    'So when are you two getting married?',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'makan mi\', artinya menikah, karena pesta nikah dulu menyajikan 잔치국수. 국수를 먹여 주다 = mengundang ke pernikahan.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'eat noodles\', meaning to marry, since weddings served 잔치국수. 국수를 먹여 주다 = invite someone to your wedding.',
  ),
  '시치미를 떼다': VocabUsage(
    '네가 먹은 거 다 알아. 시치미를 떼지 마.',
    'nega meogeun geo da ara. sichimireul tteji ma.',
    'Aku tahu kamu yang makan. Jangan pura-pura nggak tahu.',
    'I know you ate it. Don\'t play dumb.',
    'Santai (반말). Artinya pura-pura tidak tahu. Sopan: 시치미 떼지 마세요. Dalam percakapan 를 sering dihilangkan.',
    'Casual (반말). To feign ignorance. Polite: 시치미 떼지 마세요. 를 is often dropped in speech.',
  ),
  '한턱내다': VocabUsage(
    '승진했으니까 오늘은 제가 한턱내겠습니다.',
    'seungjinhaesseunikka oneureun jega hanteongnaegetseumnida.',
    'Karena saya naik jabatan, hari ini saya yang traktir.',
    'I got promoted, so today\'s on me.',
    'Formal (합니다체). Artinya mentraktir untuk merayakan sesuatu. Teman sering menagih: 한턱 쏴! (traktir dong!).',
    'Formal (합니다체). To treat people to celebrate something. Friends demand: 한턱 쏴!',
  ),
  '파김치가 되다': VocabUsage(
    '야근을 해서 파김치가 되었어요.',
    'yageuneul haeseo pagimchiga doeeosseoyo.',
    'Habis lembur, badan rasanya remuk.',
    'After working overtime, I\'m completely wiped out.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'jadi kimchi daun bawang\' yang layu, artinya sangat lelah. Bentuk lisan biasa: 파김치가 됐어요.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'become wilted green-onion kimchi\': exhausted. Spoken form: 파김치가 됐어요.',
  ),
  '오지랖이 넓다': VocabUsage(
    '옆집 아줌마는 오지랖이 넓어서 남의 일에 다 참견해요.',
    'yeopjip ajummaneun ojirapi neolbeoseo namui ire da chamgyeonhaeyo.',
    'Ibu sebelah suka ikut campur urusan orang.',
    'The lady next door is nosy and meddles in everyone\'s business.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'kelepak bajunya lebar\', artinya suka mencampuri urusan orang. Bernada kritik; jangan dipakai langsung ke orang yang lebih tua.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'one\'s coat flap is wide\': meddlesome. Critical; don\'t say it to an elder\'s face.',
  ),
  '산통을 깨다': VocabUsage(
    '깜짝 파티인데 산통을 깨지 마.',
    'kkamjjak patiinde santongeul kkaeji ma.',
    'Ini pesta kejutan, jangan dibocorkan.',
    'It\'s a surprise party, don\'t spoil it.',
    'Santai (반말). Artinya menggagalkan rencana yang hampir berhasil. Sopan: 산통을 깨지 마세요.',
    'Casual (반말). To ruin a plan that was going well. Polite: 산통을 깨지 마세요.',
  ),
  '김칫국부터 마시다': VocabUsage(
    '아직 발표도 안 났는데 김칫국부터 마시지 마세요.',
    'ajik balpyodo an nanneunde gimchitgukbuteo masiji maseyo.',
    'Pengumumannya saja belum keluar, jangan kegeeran dulu.',
    'The results aren\'t even out yet; don\'t count your chickens.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'minum kuah kimchi duluan\' sebelum kuenya datang. Dari peribahasa 떡 줄 사람은 생각도 안 하는데 김칫국부터 마신다.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'drink the kimchi broth first\' before the rice cake arrives. From 떡 줄 사람은 생각도 안 하는데 김칫국부터 마신다.',
  ),
  '찬물을 끼얹다': VocabUsage(
    '모두 신났는데 그 말이 찬물을 끼얹는 바람에 조용해졌어요.',
    'modu sinanneunde geu mari chanmureul kkieonneun barame joyonghaejyeosseoyo.',
    'Semua lagi senang, tapi omongan itu bikin suasana langsung dingin.',
    'Everyone was excited, but that remark threw cold water on it.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'menyiram air dingin\', artinya merusak suasana atau semangat orang.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'splash cold water\': kill the mood or dampen enthusiasm.',
  ),
  '물 건너가다': VocabUsage(
    '비자가 안 나와서 여행 계획은 물 건너가 버렸어요.',
    'bijaga an nawaseo yeohaeng gyehoegeun mul geonneoga beoryeosseoyo.',
    'Visanya nggak keluar, rencana liburan pun batal total.',
    'The visa didn\'t come through, so the trip plan is dead.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'sudah menyeberang air\', artinya sudah tak mungkin lagi. Biasanya bentuk lampau: 물 건너갔다.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'crossed the water\': no longer possible. Usually past tense: 물 건너갔다.',
  ),
  '뜸을 들이다': VocabUsage(
    '뜸을 들이지 말고 빨리 말해 봐.',
    'tteumeul deuriji malgo ppalli malhae bwa.',
    'Jangan bertele-tele, cepat bilang.',
    'Stop keeping me in suspense and just say it.',
    'Santai (반말). Asalnya dari menanak nasi (membiarkan nasi matang dengan uap), artinya mengulur waktu. Sopan: 뜸 들이지 말고 말해 주세요.',
    'Casual (반말). From cooking rice (letting it steam), meaning to drag things out. Polite: 뜸 들이지 말고 말해 주세요.',
  ),
  '하늘의 별 따기': VocabUsage(
    '요즘 서울에서 집 구하기는 하늘의 별 따기예요.',
    'yojeum seoureseo jip guhagineun haneurui byeol ttagiyeyo.',
    'Sekarang cari rumah di Seoul susahnya minta ampun.',
    'Finding a home in Seoul these days is next to impossible.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'memetik bintang di langit\', artinya hampir mustahil. Pola: N은/는 하늘의 별 따기다.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'picking a star from the sky\': nearly impossible. Pattern: N은/는 하늘의 별 따기다.',
  ),
  '우물 안 개구리': VocabUsage(
    '외국에 나가 보니 제가 우물 안 개구리였더라고요.',
    'oeguge naga boni jega umul an gaeguriyeotdeoragoyo.',
    'Setelah ke luar negeri, saya sadar selama ini saya katak dalam tempurung.',
    'Going abroad made me realize I\'d been a frog in a well.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'katak dalam sumur\', persis \'katak dalam tempurung\': orang berwawasan sempit.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'a frog in a well\': someone with a narrow worldview.',
  ),
  '바닥이 나다': VocabUsage(
    '월말이라 통장 잔고가 바닥이 나서 라면만 먹어요.',
    'wolmarira tongjang jangoga badagi naseo ramyeonman meogeoyo.',
    'Akhir bulan, saldo rekening habis, jadi makan mi instan saja.',
    'It\'s the end of the month and my bank balance has run dry, so I\'m living on ramen.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'sampai ke dasar\', artinya habis (uang, stok, tenaga). Mirip \'kantong kering\'.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'hit the bottom\': run out (money, stock, energy).',
  ),
  '진땀을 빼다': VocabUsage(
    '면접에서 어려운 질문 때문에 진땀을 빼고 왔어요.',
    'myeonjeobeseo eoryeoun jilmun ttaemune jinttameul ppaego wasseoyo.',
    'Di wawancara kerja, saya keringat dingin karena pertanyaan sulit.',
    'I was sweating bullets over tough questions at the interview.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'mengeluarkan keringat kental\', artinya kewalahan atau sangat gugup. Variasi: 진땀이 나다.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'shed thick sweat\': struggle hard or be very nervous. Variant: 진땀이 나다.',
  ),
  '엎질러진 물': VocabUsage(
    '이미 엎질러진 물이니까 너무 자책하지 마세요.',
    'imi eopjilleojin murinikka neomu jachaekaji maseyo.',
    'Nasi sudah menjadi bubur, jangan terlalu menyalahkan diri.',
    'It\'s no use crying over spilled milk, so don\'t blame yourself too much.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'air yang sudah tumpah\', persis \'nasi sudah menjadi bubur\'.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'spilled water\': what\'s done can\'t be undone.',
  ),
  '뒷북을 치다': VocabUsage(
    '다 끝났는데 이제 와서 뒷북을 치네.',
    'da kkeunnanneunde ije waseo dwitbugeul chine.',
    'Semua sudah selesai, baru sekarang heboh.',
    'It\'s all over and only now you react.',
    'Santai (반말). Harfiah \'memukul gendang belakangan\', artinya bereaksi atau mengabarkan hal yang sudah basi. Sopan: 뒷북을 치시네요 (tetap menyindir).',
    'Casual (반말). Literally \'beat the drum afterward\': react to old news. Polite: 뒷북을 치시네요 (still teasing).',
  ),
  '바가지를 긁다': VocabUsage(
    '아내가 매일 바가지를 긁어요.',
    'anaega maeil bagajireul geulgeoyo.',
    'Istri saya mengomel setiap hari.',
    'My wife nags me every day.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'menggaruk gayung\', artinya istri mengomeli suami. Jangan tertukar dengan 바가지를 쓰다 (kena getok).',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'scrape a gourd\': a wife nagging her husband. Don\'t confuse with 바가지를 쓰다 (get ripped off).',
  ),
  '바가지를 쓰다': VocabUsage(
    '관광지에서는 바가지를 쓰기 쉬우니까 가격을 먼저 물어보세요.',
    'gwangwangjieseoneun bagajireul sseugi swiunikka gagyeogeul meonjeo mureoboseyo.',
    'Di tempat wisata gampang kena getok harga, jadi tanya harganya dulu.',
    'It\'s easy to get ripped off at tourist spots, so ask the price first.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Artinya membayar jauh di atas harga wajar, mirip \'kena getok\'. Pelakunya: 바가지를 씌우다.',
    'Polite (해요체). To pay far more than the fair price. The one doing it: 바가지를 씌우다.',
  ),
  '땡땡이를 치다': VocabUsage(
    '고등학교 때 땡땡이를 치고 바다에 간 적이 있어요.',
    'godeunghakgyo ttae ttaengttaengireul chigo badae gan jeogi isseoyo.',
    'Waktu SMA saya pernah bolos lalu pergi ke pantai.',
    'In high school I once skipped class and went to the beach.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Bahasa lisan untuk bolos sekolah atau kerja, lebih santai dari 결석하다. 를 sering hilang: 땡땡이 치다.',
    'Polite (해요체). Colloquial for skipping school or work, more casual than 결석하다. 를 is often dropped: 땡땡이 치다.',
  ),
  '가는 말이 고와야 오는 말이 곱다': VocabUsage(
    '가는 말이 고와야 오는 말이 곱다고, 먼저 친절하게 말해 보세요.',
    'ganeun mari gowaya oneun mari gopdago, meonjeo chinjeolhage malhae boseyo.',
    'Kata yang baik dibalas kata yang baik, jadi coba bicara ramah duluan.',
    'Kind words beget kind words, so try speaking kindly first.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'kata yang pergi harus halus agar kata yang datang halus\'. Pola ~다고 dipakai untuk mengutip peribahasa sebagai alasan.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'the words going out must be gentle for the words coming back to be gentle\'. ~다고 quotes a proverb as a reason.',
  ),
  '원숭이도 나무에서 떨어진다': VocabUsage(
    '원숭이도 나무에서 떨어진다잖아요. 실수할 수도 있죠.',
    'wonsungido namueseo tteoreojindajanayo. silsuhal sudo itjyo.',
    'Sepandai-pandai tupai melompat, sekali waktu jatuh juga. Wajar kalau salah.',
    'Even monkeys fall from trees, you know. Anyone can make a mistake.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Padanan persis \'sepandai-pandai tupai melompat, sekali waktu jatuh juga\' (Korea memakai monyet). Untuk menghibur orang ahli yang berbuat salah.',
    'Polite (해요체). Even experts make mistakes; used to console a skilled person who slipped up.',
  ),
  '낮말은 새가 듣고 밤말은 쥐가 듣는다': VocabUsage(
    '낮말은 새가 듣고 밤말은 쥐가 듣는다니까 말조심하세요.',
    'nanmareun saega deutgo bammareun jwiga deunneundanikka maljosimhaseyo.',
    'Dinding pun bertelinga, jadi hati-hati bicara.',
    'Walls have ears, so watch what you say.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'omongan siang didengar burung, omongan malam didengar tikus\'. Padanan \'dinding pun bertelinga\'.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'birds hear daytime talk, mice hear nighttime talk\': someone is always listening.',
  ),
  '티끌 모아 태산': VocabUsage(
    '티끌 모아 태산이라고, 매일 천 원씩 저금하고 있어요.',
    'tikkeul moa taesanirago, maeil cheon wonssik jeogeumhago isseoyo.',
    'Sedikit demi sedikit lama-lama jadi bukit, jadi saya menabung seribu won tiap hari.',
    'Every little bit adds up, so I\'m saving a thousand won a day.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'debu dikumpulkan jadi gunung besar\', persis \'sedikit demi sedikit, lama-lama menjadi bukit\'.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'gather dust and make a great mountain\': small amounts add up.',
  ),
  '세 살 버릇 여든까지 간다': VocabUsage(
    '세 살 버릇 여든까지 간다고 하니까 어릴 때부터 습관을 잘 들여야 해요.',
    'se sal beoreut yeodeunkkaji gandago hanikka eoril ttaebuteo seupgwaneul jal deuryeoya haeyo.',
    'Kebiasaan umur tiga tahun terbawa sampai tua, jadi biasakan yang baik sejak kecil.',
    'Habits formed at three last until eighty, so build good habits early.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'kebiasaan umur tiga berlanjut sampai umur delapan puluh\'. Mirip \'kecil teranja-anja, besar terbawa-bawa\'.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'a habit at three lasts until eighty\': childhood habits stick.',
  ),
  '소 잃고 외양간 고친다': VocabUsage(
    '소 잃고 외양간 고친다고, 사고가 나기 전에 미리 점검하세요.',
    'so ilko oeyanggan gochindago, sagoga nagi jeone miri jeomgeomhaseyo.',
    'Jangan sampai menyesal kemudian; periksa dulu sebelum terjadi kecelakaan.',
    'Don\'t fix the barn after losing the cow; check things before an accident happens.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'kehilangan sapi baru memperbaiki kandang\', artinya bertindak setelah terlambat. Mirip \'sesal kemudian tiada berguna\'. Relevan untuk K3 di tempat kerja.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'fix the barn after losing the cow\': acting too late. Relevant to workplace safety.',
  ),
  '백지장도 맞들면 낫다': VocabUsage(
    '백지장도 맞들면 낫다는데 같이 해요.',
    'baekjijangdo matdeulmyeon natdaneunde gachi haeyo.',
    'Berat sama dipikul, ringan sama dijinjing. Ayo kerjakan bersama.',
    'Many hands make light work, so let\'s do it together.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'selembar kertas pun lebih ringan diangkat berdua\'. Padanan \'berat sama dipikul, ringan sama dijinjing\'.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'even a sheet of paper is easier lifted together\': cooperation helps.',
  ),
  '고래 싸움에 새우 등 터진다': VocabUsage(
    '부장님들이 싸우시니까 고래 싸움에 새우 등 터진다고 우리만 힘들어요.',
    'bujangnimdeuri ssausinikka gorae ssaume saeu deung teojindago uriman himdeureoyo.',
    'Para manajer bertengkar, kami yang di bawah kena getahnya.',
    'The managers are fighting, and we little guys are the ones who suffer.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'paus bertarung, punggung udang pecah\'. Padanan \'gajah sama gajah berjuang, pelanduk mati di tengah-tengah\'.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'whales fight and the shrimp\'s back bursts\': bystanders get hurt in big fights.',
  ),
  '공든 탑이 무너지랴': VocabUsage(
    '공든 탑이 무너지랴, 열심히 준비했으니 꼭 붙을 거예요.',
    'gongdeun tabi muneojirya, yeolsimhi junbihaesseuni kkok buteul geoyeyo.',
    'Usaha sungguh-sungguh tak akan sia-sia; kamu sudah siap, pasti lulus.',
    'Hard work never goes to waste; you prepared well, so you\'ll pass.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'menara yang dibangun dengan tekun masa runtuh?\', kalimat retoris (-랴). Untuk menyemangati sebelum ujian.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'would a carefully built tower collapse?\', a rhetorical question (-랴). Used to encourage before exams.',
  ),
  '등잔 밑이 어둡다': VocabUsage(
    '안경을 한참 찾았는데 머리 위에 있었어요. 등잔 밑이 어둡다더니!',
    'angyeongeul hancham chajanneunde meori wie isseosseoyo. deungjan michi eodupdadeoni!',
    'Kacamata saya cari lama, ternyata di atas kepala. Yang dekat malah tak kelihatan!',
    'I looked for my glasses forever and they were on my head. It\'s always darkest under the lamp!',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'di bawah pelita gelap\', artinya yang dekat justru tak terlihat. Mirip \'gajah di pelupuk mata tak tampak\'.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'it\'s dark under the lamp\': what\'s nearest is hardest to see.',
  ),
  '빈 수레가 요란하다': VocabUsage(
    '빈 수레가 요란하다더니 말만 많고 하는 일은 없네요.',
    'bin surega yoranhadadeoni malman manko haneun ireun eomneyo.',
    'Tong kosong nyaring bunyinya; banyak omong tapi nggak ada kerjanya.',
    'Empty vessels make the most noise; all talk and no action.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'gerobak kosong paling berisik\', persis \'tong kosong nyaring bunyinya\'.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'an empty cart is the noisiest\': those who know least talk most.',
  ),
  '누워서 침 뱉기': VocabUsage(
    '동료 욕을 하는 건 누워서 침 뱉기예요.',
    'dongnyo yogeul haneun geon nuwoseo chim baetgiyeyo.',
    'Menjelekkan rekan kerja sama saja menepuk air di dulang.',
    'Badmouthing coworkers is like spitting into the wind.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'meludah sambil berbaring\' (ludahnya kena muka sendiri). Padanan \'menepuk air di dulang, terpercik muka sendiri\'.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'spitting while lying down\': it lands on your own face.',
  ),
  '누워서 떡 먹기': VocabUsage(
    '그 정도 요리는 누워서 떡 먹기죠.',
    'geu jeongdo yorineun nuwoseo tteok meokgijyo.',
    'Masakan segitu sih semudah membalik telapak tangan.',
    'Cooking like that is a breeze.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'makan kue beras sambil berbaring\', artinya sangat mudah. Sama dengan 식은 죽 먹기.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'eating rice cake lying down\': very easy. Same as 식은 죽 먹기.',
  ),
  '호랑이도 제 말 하면 온다': VocabUsage(
    '호랑이도 제 말 하면 온다더니, 저기 민수 씨 오네요.',
    'horangido je mal hamyeon ondadeoni, jeogi minsu ssi oneyo.',
    'Panjang umur! Itu Minsu datang.',
    'Speak of the devil, here comes Minsu.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'harimau pun datang kalau dibicarakan\'. Padanan \'panjang umur\' saat orang yang dibicarakan muncul.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'even a tiger comes when you talk about it\'.',
  ),
  '시작이 반이다': VocabUsage(
    '시작이 반이라고 하잖아요. 일단 해 봐요.',
    'sijagi banirago hajanayo. ildan hae bwayo.',
    'Kan memulai itu sudah setengah jalan. Coba saja dulu.',
    'Well begun is half done, right? Just give it a try.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'memulai adalah separuh\', artinya bagian tersulit adalah memulai. Untuk menyemangati.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'starting is half\': the hardest part is beginning. Used to encourage.',
  ),
  '발 없는 말이 천 리 간다': VocabUsage(
    '발 없는 말이 천 리 간다니까 소문 조심해요.',
    'bal eomneun mari cheolli gandanikka somun josimhaeyo.',
    'Kabar cepat sekali menyebar, jadi hati-hati dengan gosip.',
    'Word travels fast, so be careful with rumors.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Permainan kata: 말 = \'kata\' dan \'kuda\'. Harfiah \'kata tanpa kaki pergi seribu li\'.',
    'Polite (해요체). Wordplay: 말 means both \'word\' and \'horse\'. Literally \'a word without feet travels a thousand li\'.',
  ),
  '금강산도 식후경': VocabUsage(
    '금강산도 식후경이라는데 밥부터 먹고 구경해요.',
    'geumgangsando sikugyeongiraneunde bapbuteo meokgo gugyeonghaeyo.',
    'Seindah apa pun pemandangan, makan dulu. Ayo makan, baru jalan-jalan.',
    'Even Mt. Geumgang comes after a meal, so let\'s eat first, then look around.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'Gunung Geumgang pun dinikmati setelah makan\', artinya perut diisi dulu. Populer saat jalan-jalan.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'even Mt. Geumgang is viewed after eating\': food first. Popular when sightseeing.',
  ),
  '하늘이 무너져도 솟아날 구멍이 있다': VocabUsage(
    '하늘이 무너져도 솟아날 구멍이 있다고, 포기하지 마세요.',
    'haneuri muneojyeodo sosanal gumeongi itdago, pogihaji maseyo.',
    'Sesulit apa pun pasti ada jalan keluar, jangan menyerah.',
    'Even if the sky falls there\'s a way out, so don\'t give up.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'langit runtuh pun ada lubang untuk keluar\'. Mirip \'di mana ada kemauan, di situ ada jalan\'.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'even if the sky collapses, there is a hole to escape through\'.',
  ),
  '벼는 익을수록 고개를 숙인다': VocabUsage(
    '벼는 익을수록 고개를 숙인다고, 그분은 정말 겸손하세요.',
    'byeoneun igeulsurok gogaereul sugindago, geubuneun jeongmal gyeomsonhaseyo.',
    'Seperti ilmu padi, makin berisi makin merunduk; beliau sungguh rendah hati.',
    'Like ripe rice bowing its head, he\'s truly humble.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'padi makin matang makin menunduk\', persis \'ilmu padi\'.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'the riper the rice, the lower it bows\': the wiser, the humbler.',
  ),
  '웃는 얼굴에 침 못 뱉는다': VocabUsage(
    '웃는 얼굴에 침 못 뱉는다고, 웃으면서 부탁하니까 거절을 못 했어요.',
    'unneun eolgure chim mot baenneundago, useumyeonseo butakanikka geojeoreul motaesseoyo.',
    'Orang yang tersenyum sulit dimarahi; dia minta tolong sambil senyum, jadi saya tak bisa menolak.',
    'You can\'t spit on a smiling face; he asked with a smile, so I couldn\'t say no.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'tak bisa meludahi wajah yang tersenyum\', artinya sikap ramah meluluhkan orang.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'you can\'t spit on a smiling face\': friendliness disarms people.',
  ),
  '개구리 올챙이 적 생각 못 한다': VocabUsage(
    '개구리 올챙이 적 생각 못 한다더니, 신입 때를 벌써 잊었어요?',
    'gaeguri olchaengi jeok saenggak motandadeoni, sinip ttaereul beolsseo ijeosseoyo?',
    'Kacang lupa kulitnya; sudah lupa masa jadi karyawan baru?',
    'Forgot where you came from? Have you already forgotten your rookie days?',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'katak tak ingat masa jadi kecebong\'. Padanan \'kacang lupa kulitnya\'.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'the frog forgets its tadpole days\'.',
  ),
  '꿩 먹고 알 먹고': VocabUsage(
    '운동도 하고 돈도 벌고, 꿩 먹고 알 먹고네요.',
    'undongdo hago dondo beolgo, kkwong meokgo al meokgoneyo.',
    'Olahraga dapat, uang pun dapat. Sekali dayung, dua pulau terlampaui.',
    'Getting exercise and earning money: two birds with one stone.',
    'Sopan (해요체). Harfiah \'makan burung pegar sekaligus telurnya\'. Padanan \'sekali dayung, dua tiga pulau terlampaui\'. Sinonim: 일석이조.',
    'Polite (해요체). Literally \'eat the pheasant and its eggs too\'. Synonym: 일석이조.',
  ),
  '돌다리도 두들겨 보고 건너라': VocabUsage(
    '돌다리도 두들겨 보고 건너라고, 계약서를 꼼꼼히 읽어 보세요.',
    'doldarido dudeulgyeo bogo geonneorago, gyeyakseoreul kkomkkomhi ilgeo boseyo.',
    'Hati-hati sebelum melangkah; baca kontraknya dengan teliti.',
    'Look before you leap; read the contract carefully.',
